            <!-- 1.0 INTRODUCTION -->
            <section class="card" id="section-1">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <h2 class="card-title mb-0">1.0 Introduction</h2>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h3 id="section-1-1">1.1 Purpose</h3>
                    <p>This Software Requirements Specification (SRS) presents a detailed description of the <strong>KlashOut</strong> platform. It explains the purpose and features of the system, user interfaces, system behavior, constraints, and how the system will react to external stimuli.</p>

                    <p><strong>Intended Audience:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Stakeholders</strong> (Lincoln, Grace, investors) — For approval and business alignment</li>
                        <li><strong>Developers</strong> (Phase 2 implementation team) — For technical implementation guidance</li>
                        <li><strong>Legal/Compliance</strong> — For regulatory review (FCA, GDPR, App Store)</li>
                        <li><strong>Project Managers</strong> — For milestone planning and estimation</li>
                    </ul>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h3 id="section-1-2" class="mt-3">1.2 Scope of Project</h3>
                    <p>KlashOut is a <strong>sound clash competition platform</strong> that digitizes the Jamaican DJ/soundsystem tradition of head-to-head musical battles. The platform allows users to compete in real-time klashes (music battles), with audiences deciding winners through voting and engagement.</p>

                    <h4 class="mt-3">What the System Will Do</h4>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Core Game Loop:</strong> Match users by genre/skill, play competing music tracks simultaneously, audience votes in real-time, declare winner, award points/coins</li>
                        <li><strong>Tiered Monetization:</strong> Three user tiers (Klasher, Independent Klasher, Super Klasher) with increasing features and revenue opportunities</li>
                        <li><strong>Virtual Economy:</strong> 1:1 fiat-backed "Klash Coin" for tipping, music purchases, tournament entry fees, and cash-out</li>
                        <li><strong>Social Layer:</strong> Profiles, followers, playlists, messaging, forums, discovery feeds</li>
                        <li><strong>Advanced Features:</strong> Tournaments, Go Live showcases, nudge play mechanics, music social sharing</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h4 class="mt-3">What the System Will NOT Do (Out of Scope)</h4>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Music streaming service (users upload tracks, system does not license from labels)</li>
                        <li>Audio production/editing tools</li>
                        <li>Blockchain/cryptocurrency implementation (1:1 fiat-backed wallet only)</li>
                        <li>Physical hardware integration</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h4 class="mt-3">Success Criteria</h4>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Phase 1 Target:</strong> Support 10,000-50,000 concurrent users (comfortable limit)</li>
                        <li><strong>Long-Term Target:</strong> Scale to 2 million total users</li>
                        <li><strong>Performance:</strong> ≤200ms real-time event delivery for voting/game state</li>
                        <li><strong>Financial Integrity:</strong> Zero unbalanced wallet transactions (ACID compliance)</li>
                        <li><strong>Regulatory:</strong> FCA e-money compliance via licensed partner</li>
                    </ul>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h3 id="section-1-3" class="mt-3">1.3 Glossary</h3>
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Term</th>
                                <th>Definition</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Klash</strong></td>
                                <td>A real-time music battle between two or more users, with audience voting to determine winner</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Klasher</strong></td>
                                <td>Basic tier user who can participate in klashes with limited features</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Independent Klasher</strong></td>
                                <td>Mid-tier user who can upload original music, sell tracks, and access advanced features</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Super Klasher</strong></td>
                                <td>Premium tier user who can host tournaments (Super Klashes) with unlimited participants and entry fees</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Klash Coin</strong></td>
                                <td>Platform currency; 1:1 fiat-backed (£1 = 1 Klash Coin), used for tipping, purchases, entry fees</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Spectator</strong></td>
                                <td>User watching a klash; can vote, gift coins, and chat</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Go Live</strong></td>
                                <td>Special klash mode where spectators pay to have their track played during the battle</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Nudge Play</strong></td>
                                <td>Tactical mechanic in 60/90-second klashes (mechanic details pending stakeholder definition)</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Super Klash</strong></td>
                                <td>Tournament-style klash hosted by Super Klasher with entry fees, pot, and prize distribution</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Genre</strong></td>
                                <td>Music category (Reggae, Metal, House, Punk, Soul, Rock, R&B, Indie, Jazz, Hip Hop, International, Classical, Pop, UK Underground)</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Matchmaking</strong></td>
                                <td>System-automated opponent pairing based on genre preference and skill/tier</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Direct Challenge</strong></td>
                                <td>User-initiated klash invitation to specific opponent</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>

                    <p class="mt-3"><strong>See Also:</strong> <a href="reference.html">Reference Tables</a> for complete genre list, transaction types, and technical constants</p>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

