                    <h4 class="mt-3">Traceability Notation</h4>
                    <p>Requirements are traced using the following notation:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Epic X</strong> — High-level feature grouping (12 epics total)</li>
                        <li><strong>F##</strong> — Functional requirement / user story (F01-F45)</li>
                        <li><strong>NF##</strong> — Non-functional requirement (NF01-NF10)</li>
                        <li><strong>D##</strong> — Domain requirement (regulatory, compliance)</li>
                        <li><strong>C##</strong> — Conflict (documented contradiction)</li>
                        <li><strong>Q#.#</strong> — Open question for stakeholder</li>
                        <li><strong>DD-###</strong> — Design decision</li>
                    </ul>

                    <p class="mt-3"><strong>Example Cross-Reference:</strong><br>
                    <em>"The wallet system (Epic 8, F48-F52) requires ACID transactions (NF06) to satisfy FCA e-money regulations (D02). The fiat-backed approach resolves C01. Implementation details in DD-003."</em></p>
