            <!-- 2.0 OVERALL DESCRIPTION -->
            <section class="card" id="section-2">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <h2 class="card-title mb-0">2.0 Overall Description</h2>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p class="alert alert-info">This section describes the system from a <strong>stakeholder perspective</strong> using non-technical language. For detailed technical specifications, see <a href="#section-3">Section 3</a>.</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- 2.1 Product Perspective -->
            <section class="card" id="section-2-1">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <h3 class="card-title mb-0">2.1 Product Perspective</h3>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h4>What is Sound Clash?</h4>
                    <p>Sound clash is a <strong>Jamaican DJ/soundsystem tradition</strong> where two competing sound systems go head-to-head playing music, with the audience deciding the winner through applause, airhorns, and crowd energy. KlashOut digitizes this cultural phenomenon into a global, real-time, gamified platform.</p>

                    <h4 class="mt-3">System Environment</h4>
                    <p>KlashOut consists of:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Web Application</strong> — React-based responsive web app (primary Phase 1 deliverable)</li>
                        <li><strong>Mobile Application</strong> — React Native iOS/Android apps (simultaneous development with web)</li>
                        <li><strong>API Backend</strong> — Node.js REST API + WebSockets (client-agnostic)</li>
                        <li><strong>Database</strong> — PostgreSQL (relational, ACID-compliant)</li>
                        <li><strong>File Storage</strong> — Cloudflare R2 for music files (S3-compatible, zero egress fees)</li>
                        <li><strong>Payment Provider</strong> — Stripe Connect or Mangopay (FCA-licensed e-money partner)</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h4 class="mt-3">Target Audience</h4>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Primary:</strong> Music enthusiasts aged 18-35 in UK/US markets</li>
                        <li><strong>Secondary:</strong> Independent artists seeking audience and monetization</li>
                        <li><strong>Tertiary:</strong> Sound system operators and DJs (nostalgic for physical clashes)</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h4 class="mt-3">Competitive Positioning</h4>
                    <p>KlashOut occupies a unique niche:</p>
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Competitor</th>
                                <th>What They Offer</th>
                                <th>KlashOut Difference</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Spotify</strong></td>
                                <td>Music streaming</td>
                                <td>Not streaming — competitive social experience</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>TikTok</strong></td>
                                <td>Short-form video + music</td>
                                <td>Real-time head-to-head battles, not asynchronous posts</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Twitch</strong></td>
                                <td>Live streaming + chat</td>
                                <td>Gamified competition with points/coins, not passive viewing</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>SoundCloud</strong></td>
                                <td>Artist uploads + discovery</td>
                                <td>Competitive validation (win = proof of quality)</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>

                    <p class="mt-3"><strong>Key Innovation:</strong> KlashOut is the <strong>only platform</strong> combining real-time music competition, audience voting, and cryptocurrency-free virtual economy (1:1 fiat-backed).</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- 2.2 User Roles & Characteristics -->
            <section class="card" id="section-2-2">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <h3 class="card-title mb-0">2.2 User Roles & Characteristics</h3>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p>KlashOut has four primary user roles, each with distinct characteristics and system interactions:</p>

                    <h4>1. Klasher (Basic Tier) <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span></h4>
                    <p><strong>Profile:</strong> Entry-level user; music enthusiast, casual competitor</p>
                    <p><strong>Technical Skill:</strong> Low — expects intuitive mobile/web interface</p>
                    <p><strong>Primary Goals:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Participate in music battles (klashes)</li>
                        <li>Vote on other users' klashes as spectator</li>
                        <li>Build reputation through wins and points</li>
                        <li>Discover new music and connect with similar tastes</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>System Permissions:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>✅ Join klashes (as participant or spectator)</li>
                        <li>✅ Vote in klashes</li>
                        <li>✅ Create playlists from platform library</li>
                        <li>✅ Send/receive Klash Coins (gifts, winnings)</li>
                        <li>❌ Upload original music</li>
                        <li>❌ Sell tracks</li>
                        <li>❌ Host tournaments</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>Monetization:</strong> Free tier (no subscription)</p>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h4 class="mt-3">2. Independent Klasher (Mid Tier) <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span></h4>
                    <p><strong>Profile:</strong> Independent artist, producer, serious music creator</p>
                    <p><strong>Technical Skill:</strong> Medium — comfortable with file uploads, payments, analytics</p>
                    <p><strong>Primary Goals:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Showcase original music to audience</li>
                        <li>Monetize tracks through direct sales</li>
                        <li>Build fanbase and following</li>
                        <li>Gain competitive validation (wins = proof of quality)</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>System Permissions:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>✅ All Klasher permissions</li>
                        <li>✅ Upload original music (MP3, WAV, FLAC)</li>
                        <li>✅ Set track prices (Klash Coins)</li>
                        <li>✅ Earn revenue from track sales</li>
                        <li>✅ Analytics dashboard (plays, purchases, earnings)</li>
                        <li>✅ Participate in Go Live showcases</li>
                        <li>❌ Host Super Klashes (tournaments)</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>Monetization:</strong> Revenue share model (platform takes % of sales) OR subscription (TBD — see Q8.4)</p>
                    <p><strong>Upgrade Criteria:</strong> ⚠️ UNDEFINED — requires stakeholder input (see <a href="questions-for-lincoln.html#Q1.4">Q1.4</a>)</p>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h4 class="mt-3">3. Super Klasher (Premium Tier) <span class="badge badge-could-have">COULD HAVE</span></h4>
                    <p><strong>Profile:</strong> Power user, event organizer, influencer, professional DJ</p>
                    <p><strong>Technical Skill:</strong> High — manages tournaments, finances, large audiences</p>
                    <p><strong>Primary Goals:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Host large-scale tournaments (Super Klashes)</li>
                        <li>Earn hosting fees and revenue share from prize pools</li>
                        <li>Build community around events</li>
                        <li>Professional reputation as event curator</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>System Permissions:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>✅ All Independent Klasher permissions</li>
                        <li>✅ Host Super Klashes (tournaments with unlimited participants)</li>
                        <li>✅ Set entry fees for tournaments</li>
                        <li>✅ Collect hosting fee % from prize pool</li>
                        <li>✅ Access to advanced analytics (participant demographics, engagement metrics)</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>Monetization:</strong> Hosting fee revenue + possible subscription (TBD)</p>
                    <p><strong>Upgrade Criteria:</strong> ⚠️ UNDEFINED — possible thresholds: 1,000 followers + 1,000 wins (see <a href="payment-tiers.html">Payment Tiers</a>)</p>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h4 class="mt-3">4. Spectator (Non-Participant Role)</h4>
                    <p><strong>Profile:</strong> Any authenticated user observing a klash without competing</p>
                    <p><strong>Technical Skill:</strong> Low — passive consumption with optional engagement</p>
                    <p><strong>Primary Goals:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Watch live klashes for entertainment</li>
                        <li>Vote to influence outcomes</li>
                        <li>Discover new music and artists</li>
                        <li>Tip performers with Klash Coins</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>System Permissions:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>✅ Browse active klashes via forums</li>
                        <li>✅ Vote for preferred competitor</li>
                        <li>✅ Chat during klash (if enabled)</li>
                        <li>✅ Gift Klash Coins to competitors</li>
                        <li>✅ Participate in Go Live (pay to have track played)</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>Note:</strong> Spectator is a <strong>contextual role</strong> — any Klasher/Independent/Super user becomes a spectator when observing a klash they're not competing in.</p>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h4 class="mt-3">User Characteristics Summary</h4>
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Characteristic</th>
                                <th>Klasher</th>
                                <th>Independent</th>
                                <th>Super Klasher</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Age Range</strong></td>
                                <td>18-35 (primary)</td>
                                <td>22-40 (creators)</td>
                                <td>25-50 (organizers)</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Technical Expertise</strong></td>
                                <td>Low (mobile-first)</td>
                                <td>Medium (upload, analytics)</td>
                                <td>High (event management)</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Time Commitment</strong></td>
                                <td>Casual (5-30 min sessions)</td>
                                <td>Regular (weekly uploads)</td>
                                <td>Dedicated (event planning)</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Monetization Focus</strong></td>
                                <td>None (win for prestige)</td>
                                <td>High (sell music)</td>
                                <td>High (hosting fees)</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Expected Platform Use</strong></td>
                                <td>Mobile app (70%), Web (30%)</td>
                                <td>Web (60%), Mobile (40%)</td>
                                <td>Web (80%), Mobile (20%)</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>

                    <p class="mt-3"><strong>Accessibility Requirements:</strong> All user roles must be supported on both web and mobile platforms (NF07). See <a href="system-design.html">System Design Document</a> for API-first architecture supporting cross-platform access.</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- 2.3 Functional Overview (12 Epics) -->
            <section class="card" id="section-2-3">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <h3 class="card-title mb-0">2.3 Functional Overview (12 Epics)</h3>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p>KlashOut functionality is organized into <strong>12 epics</strong> (high-level feature groupings). This section provides a stakeholder-friendly overview of each epic. For detailed user stories and acceptance criteria, see <a href="#section-3-2">Section 3.2</a> and <a href="epic-hierarchy.html">Epic Hierarchy</a>.</p>

                    <h4>Epic 1: User Account Management <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span></h4>
                    <p><strong>What it does:</strong> Allows users to create accounts, log in, manage profiles, and control privacy settings.</p>
                    <p><strong>Why it's critical:</strong> Foundation for all other features. Every user must authenticate before using the platform.</p>
                    <p><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Registration with email/password or OAuth (Google, Apple, Facebook)</li>
                        <li>JWT-based authentication with refresh tokens</li>
                        <li>Profile creation (Klasher name, bio, profile image)</li>
                        <li>Tier assignment (Klasher / Independent / Super)</li>
                        <li>Privacy controls (public/private profile, blocking users)</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>User Stories:</strong> F01-F05 (5 stories)</p>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h4 class="mt-3">Epic 2: Music Library & Song Selection <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span></h4>
                    <p><strong>What it does:</strong> Manages music uploads, storage, streaming, and genre categorization.</p>
                    <p><strong>Why it's critical:</strong> No music = no klashes. This is the content layer.</p>
                    <p><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Music file upload (MP3, WAV, FLAC) — Independent/Super only</li>
                        <li>Genre tagging (14 predefined genres)</li>
                        <li>Track metadata (artist, title, duration, BPM)</li>
                        <li>Streaming with CDN delivery (Cloudflare R2)</li>
                        <li>Browse/search library by genre, artist, popularity</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>User Stories:</strong> F06-F10 (5 stories)</p>
                    <p><strong>Domain Requirement:</strong> D01 — Music licensing compliance (see <a href="#section-2-6">Section 2.6</a>)</p>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h4 class="mt-3">Epic 3: Klashing (Core Game Loop) <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span></h4>
                    <p><strong>What it does:</strong> The core competition mechanic — matchmaking, real-time battles, voting, results.</p>
                    <p><strong>Why it's critical:</strong> This IS the product. Everything else supports this.</p>
                    <p><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Matchmaking by genre and skill level</li>
                        <li>Real-time klash state (WebSockets for <200ms latency)</li>
                        <li>Simultaneous audio playback for competitors</li>
                        <li>Live voting by spectators</li>
                        <li>Winner determination (vote tally OR algorithmic — see C02)</li>
                        <li>Points and coin rewards distribution</li>
                        <li>Klash duration: 30s, 60s, 90s, 2min, 3min</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>User Stories:</strong> F11-F20 (10 stories)</p>
                    <p><strong>Open Items:</strong> C02 (winner logic), Q2.1 (voting vs algorithm), Q3.1 (concurrent ceiling)</p>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h4 class="mt-3">Epic 4: Tournaments & Super Klashes <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span></h4>
                    <p><strong>What it does:</strong> Multi-round competitive formats with entry fees and prize pools.</p>
                    <p><strong>Why it's valuable:</strong> Drives engagement and monetization; appeals to competitive users.</p>
                    <p><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Tournament formats: Swiss, Single Elimination, Double Elimination</li>
                        <li>Super Klash hosting (Super Klasher exclusive)</li>
                        <li>Entry fee collection (Klash Coins)</li>
                        <li>Prize pool distribution (1st, 2nd, 3rd + host fee)</li>
                        <li>Bracket visualization and live standings</li>
                        <li>Unlimited participants (scalability challenge — see C04)</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>User Stories:</strong> F21-F25 (5 stories)</p>
                    <p><strong>Open Items:</strong> Q9.1 (pot split percentages), Q4.1 (tournament bracket limits)</p>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h4 class="mt-3">Epic 5: Profile & Social Feed <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span></h4>
                    <p><strong>What it does:</strong> User profiles, stats aggregation, activity feeds, follower system.</p>
                    <p><strong>Why it's valuable:</strong> Social proof and discovery; users need identity and reputation.</p>
                    <p><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Public profile page (stats, recent klashes, uploaded tracks)</li>
                        <li>Aggregated statistics (win rate, total points, klashes played)</li>
                        <li>Follower/following system</li>
                        <li>Activity feed (followed users' klashes, wins, uploads)</li>
                        <li>Leaderboards (global, genre-specific, weekly)</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>User Stories:</strong> F26-F30 (5 stories)</p>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h4 class="mt-3">Epic 6: Messaging <span class="badge badge-could-have">COULD HAVE</span></h4>
                    <p><strong>What it does:</strong> Direct messages between users, chat during klashes.</p>
                    <p><strong>Why it's nice-to-have:</strong> Standard social feature but not blocking for launch.</p>
                    <p><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>1:1 direct messaging</li>
                        <li>Klash chat rooms (participants + spectators)</li>
                        <li>Profanity filtering (Q10.1 — moderation approach TBD)</li>
                        <li>Message history and notifications</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>User Stories:</strong> F31-F33 (3 stories)</p>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h4 class="mt-3">Epic 7: Playlists <span class="badge badge-could-have">COULD HAVE</span></h4>
                    <p><strong>What it does:</strong> Users create playlists for klash preparation.</p>
                    <p><strong>Why it's valuable:</strong> Organization tool; helps users prepare track selections.</p>
                    <p><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Create/update/delete playlists</li>
                        <li>Add tracks from library to playlist</li>
                        <li>Playlist ordering and categorization</li>
                        <li>Load playlist into klash song selection</li>
                        <li>Share playlists with followers</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>User Stories:</strong> F34-F36 (3 stories)</p>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h4 class="mt-3">Epic 8: Wallet & Klash Coin <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span></h4>
                    <p><strong>What it does:</strong> Virtual economy — top-up, gifting, purchases, cash-out.</p>
                    <p><strong>Why it's critical:</strong> Monetization backbone; enables all financial transactions.</p>
                    <p><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>1:1 fiat-backed wallet (£1 = 1 Klash Coin)</li>
                        <li>Top-up via credit/debit card (Stripe integration)</li>
                        <li>Gift coins to other users (during klash or passively)</li>
                        <li>Purchase tracks from Independent Klashers</li>
                        <li>Super Klash entry fees and prize distribution</li>
                        <li>Cash-out to bank account (minimum threshold TBD — see Q6.2)</li>
                        <li>Transaction history and balance tracking</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>User Stories:</strong> F37-F41 (5 stories) + F48-F52 (new transaction types)</p>
                    <p><strong>Domain Requirement:</strong> D02 — FCA e-money compliance via licensed partner</p>
                    <p><strong>NFR:</strong> NF06 — ACID transactions, zero unbalanced movements</p>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h4 class="mt-3">Epic 9: Go Live Showcases <span class="badge badge-could-have">COULD HAVE</span></h4>
                    <p><strong>What it does:</strong> Spectators pay to have their track played during a live klash.</p>
                    <p><strong>Why it's valuable:</strong> Unique monetization mechanic; creates "pay-to-participate" moments.</p>
                    <p><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Go Live activation 10 seconds into klash (not last 10 seconds)</li>
                        <li>Spectators pay Klash Coins to queue their track</li>
                        <li>Track plays for 15-30 seconds</li>
                        <li>Coins distributed to klash participants</li>
                        <li>Go Live Showcase (Independent artists pay before klash to perform)</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>User Stories:</strong> F42 (1 story) + updates from Coin Wallet doc</p>
                    <p><strong>Open Items:</strong> Q8.1 (Go Live Showcase monetization)</p>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h4 class="mt-3">Epic 10: Nudge Play <span class="badge badge-blocked">BLOCKED</span></h4>
                    <p><strong>What it does:</strong> ⚠️ UNDEFINED — mechanic not specified in source documents.</p>
                    <p><strong>Why it's blocked:</strong> Cannot design without knowing what "nudge" actually does.</p>
                    <p><strong>Mentioned in:</strong> Wallet & Coin UX doc (transaction type), Gaming Mechanic doc (60/90s klashes only)</p>
                    <p><strong>Possible Interpretations:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Interrupt opponent's audio playback</li>
                        <li>Tactical 3-use mechanic (like Mario Kart items)</li>
                        <li>Join ongoing klash mid-battle</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>User Stories:</strong> F53 (placeholder — requires definition)</p>
                    <p><strong>Open Items:</strong> Q2.2 (BLOCKING — must define mechanic)</p>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h4 class="mt-3">Epic 11: Forums & Discovery <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span></h4>
                    <p><strong>What it does:</strong> Browse active klashes, genre-based forums, spectator entry points.</p>
                    <p><strong>Why it's valuable:</strong> Discovery layer; users need to find klashes to spectate.</p>
                    <p><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Genre-based forum pages (one per genre)</li>
                        <li>Live klash browser (active/upcoming battles)</li>
                        <li>Filter by skill level, duration, entry fee</li>
                        <li>Join as spectator with one click</li>
                        <li>"BK" feature (undefined term — see Q6.1)</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>User Stories:</strong> F54-F56 (3 stories)</p>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h4 class="mt-3">Epic 12: Music Social (Snippet Messaging) <span class="badge badge-wont-have">WON'T HAVE (Phase 1)</span></h4>
                    <p><strong>What it does:</strong> Send music snippets in messages, emotion-based recommendations.</p>
                    <p><strong>Why it's deferred:</strong> Advanced feature requiring recommendation engine; Phase 2+.</p>
                    <p><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Attach 30-second track snippets to messages</li>
                        <li>Emotion-based music tagging (happy, sad, energetic, chill)</li>
                        <li>Recommendation engine based on listening history</li>
                        <li>Shareable snippet links (social media integration)</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>User Stories:</strong> F57-F59 (3 stories)</p>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h4 class="mt-3">Epic Summary Table</h4>
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Epic</th>
                                <th>Priority</th>
                                <th>User Stories</th>
                                <th>Status</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Epic 1:</strong> User Accounts</td>
                                <td><span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span></td>
                                <td>F01-F05</td>
                                <td>✅ Fully specified</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Epic 2:</strong> Music Library</td>
                                <td><span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span></td>
                                <td>F06-F10</td>
                                <td>⚠️ Requires D01 licensing</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Epic 3:</strong> Klashing</td>
                                <td><span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span></td>
                                <td>F11-F20</td>
                                <td>⚠️ C02 (winner logic) open</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Epic 4:</strong> Tournaments</td>
                                <td><span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span></td>
                                <td>F21-F25</td>
                                <td>⚠️ Q9.1 (pot %) open</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Epic 5:</strong> Profile & Feed</td>
                                <td><span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span></td>
                                <td>F26-F30</td>
                                <td>✅ Fully specified</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Epic 6:</strong> Messaging</td>
                                <td><span class="badge badge-could-have">COULD HAVE</span></td>
                                <td>F31-F33</td>
                                <td>⚠️ Q10.1 (moderation) open</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Epic 7:</strong> Playlists</td>
                                <td><span class="badge badge-could-have">COULD HAVE</span></td>
                                <td>F34-F36</td>
                                <td>✅ Fully specified</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Epic 8:</strong> Wallet</td>
                                <td><span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span></td>
                                <td>F37-F52</td>
                                <td>✅ C01 resolved (fiat-backed)</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Epic 9:</strong> Go Live</td>
                                <td><span class="badge badge-could-have">COULD HAVE</span></td>
                                <td>F42</td>
                                <td>⚠️ Q8.1 (monetization) open</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Epic 10:</strong> Nudge Play</td>
                                <td><span class="badge badge-blocked">BLOCKED</span></td>
                                <td>F53</td>
                                <td>🔴 Q2.2 BLOCKING</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Epic 11:</strong> Forums</td>
                                <td><span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span></td>
                                <td>F54-F56</td>
                                <td>⚠️ "BK" term undefined</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Epic 12:</strong> Music Social</td>
                                <td><span class="badge badge-wont-have">WON'T HAVE</span></td>
                                <td>F57-F59</td>
                                <td>⏸️ Deferred to Phase 2+</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>

                    <p class="mt-3"><strong>For detailed epic breakdown and build order, see:</strong> <a href="epic-hierarchy.html">Epic Hierarchy & Build Order</a></p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- 2.4 Non-Functional Requirements (High-Level) -->
            <section class="card" id="section-2-4">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <h3 class="card-title mb-0">2.4 Non-Functional Requirements (High-Level)</h3>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p>Non-functional requirements (NFRs) define <strong>how the system performs</strong>, not what it does. This section provides stakeholder-friendly NFR summaries. For detailed measurable targets, see <a href="#section-3-3">Section 3.3</a>.</p>

                    <h4>Performance & Scalability</h4>
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Requirement</th>
                                <th>Target</th>
                                <th>Why It Matters</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>NF01:</strong> Web page load time</td>
                                <td>≤2 seconds (p95)</td>
                                <td>Users abandon sites after 3 seconds</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>NF02:</strong> Real-time event latency</td>
                                <td>≤200ms (voting, game state)</td>
                                <td>Voting must feel instant for competitive integrity</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>NF03:</strong> Concurrent users (Phase 1)</td>
                                <td>10,000-50,000 users</td>
                                <td>Initial comfortable ceiling; must scale to 2M long-term</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>NF04:</strong> Database query time</td>
                                <td>≤100ms (p95)</td>
                                <td>Keeps UI responsive under load</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>

                    <h4 class="mt-3">Reliability & Availability</h4>
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Requirement</th>
                                <th>Target</th>
                                <th>Why It Matters</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>NF05:</strong> System uptime</td>
                                <td>99.5% (43.8 hours downtime/year)</td>
                                <td>Acceptable for Phase 1; upgrade to 99.9% for Phase 2</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>NF06:</strong> Financial transaction integrity</td>
                                <td>100% ACID compliance</td>
                                <td>Zero tolerance for unbalanced wallet movements (regulatory)</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>

                    <h4 class="mt-3">Security</h4>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Authentication:</strong> JWT tokens with 15-minute expiry + refresh tokens</li>
                        <li><strong>Password storage:</strong> bcrypt with cost factor 12 (minimum)</li>
                        <li><strong>HTTPS enforcement:</strong> All traffic encrypted in transit (TLS 1.3)</li>
                        <li><strong>Input validation:</strong> Server-side validation on all user inputs (prevent XSS, SQL injection)</li>
                        <li><strong>Payment security:</strong> PCI DSS compliance via Stripe/Mangopay (no card data stored)</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h4 class="mt-3">Cross-Platform Support</h4>
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Platform</th>
                                <th>Requirements</th>
                                <th>Priority</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Web (Desktop)</strong></td>
                                <td>Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge (latest 2 versions)</td>
                                <td><span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Web (Mobile)</strong></td>
                                <td>Responsive design, touch-optimized</td>
                                <td><span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>iOS App</strong></td>
                                <td>iOS 14+ (iPhone, iPad)</td>
                                <td><span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Android App</strong></td>
                                <td>Android 8.0+ (Oreo)</td>
                                <td><span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span></td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>

                    <h4 class="mt-3">File Size Limits</h4>
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Asset Type</th>
                                <th>Maximum Size</th>
                                <th>Rationale</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Music uploads</strong></td>
                                <td>50MB per file</td>
                                <td>Supports high-quality FLAC; prevents abuse</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Profile images</strong></td>
                                <td>5MB per file</td>
                                <td>Standard for high-resolution photos</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>

                    <p class="mt-3"><strong>Complete NFR specifications:</strong> See <a href="reference.html">Reference Tables</a> and <a href="#section-3-3">Section 3.3</a> for measurable targets and test criteria.</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- 2.5 Payment Tiers & Monetization -->
            <section class="card" id="section-2-5">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <h3 class="card-title mb-0">2.5 Payment Tiers & Monetization</h3>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="alert alert-warning">
                        <div class="alert-title">⚠️ Pricing & Upgrade Mechanisms Undefined</div>
                        <p>This section describes the <strong>tier structure</strong>, but critical monetization details are undefined in source documents. The following questions require stakeholder input:</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li><strong>Q1.4:</strong> How do users upgrade between tiers? (Achievement, payment, application)</li>
                            <li><strong>Q8.4:</strong> What are subscription prices (if applicable)?</li>
                            <li><strong>Q8.5:</strong> Can users hold multiple tiers simultaneously?</li>
                            <li><strong>Q8.6:</strong> Mobile pricing strategy (15-30% app store commission)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>

                    <h4>Tier Structure Overview</h4>
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Tier</th>
                                <th>Color Code</th>
                                <th>Key Permissions</th>
                                <th>Monetization Model</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Klasher</strong></td>
                                <td>Blue</td>
                                <td>Compete, vote, spectate, follow</td>
                                <td><strong>Free</strong> (no subscription)</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Independent Klasher</strong></td>
                                <td>Gold</td>
                                <td>+ Upload music, sell tracks, Go Live Showcase</td>
                                <td><strong>Revenue share</strong> OR subscription (TBD)</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Super Klasher</strong></td>
                                <td>Pink</td>
                                <td>+ Host tournaments, unlimited participants, hosting fees</td>
                                <td><strong>Hosting fee %</strong> + possible subscription (TBD)</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>

                    <h4 class="mt-3">Revenue Streams</h4>

                    <h5>1. Klash Coin Transactions (Platform Fee)</h5>
                    <p>KlashOut earns a percentage on all Klash Coin transactions:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Top-up:</strong> Payment processor fee (Stripe: 2.9% + £0.30) — platform absorbs or passes to user (TBD)</li>
                        <li><strong>Music purchases:</strong> % of sale price (exact % TBD)</li>
                        <li><strong>Gifting:</strong> Possible small fee (TBD)</li>
                        <li><strong>Cash-out:</strong> Possible withdrawal fee or minimum threshold (TBD — see Q6.2)</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h5 class="mt-3">2. Super Klash Hosting Fees</h5>
                    <p><strong>Source:</strong> RD document for Rohit Coin Wallet (27 May 2026)</p>
                    <blockquote>
                        <p>"The SK takes a percentage of the hosting fee and a percentage of the winnings"</p>
                    </blockquote>
                    <p><strong>⚠️ UNDEFINED:</strong> Exact percentages not specified (see Q8.3).</p>

                    <p><strong>How it works:</strong></p>
                    <ol>
                        <li>Super Klasher sets entry fee (e.g., 10 Klash Coins)</li>
                        <li>100 participants enter → 1,000 coins in pot</li>
                        <li>Platform takes X% hosting fee</li>
                        <li>Super Klasher takes Y% of remaining pot</li>
                        <li>1st, 2nd, 3rd place split remaining coins</li>
                    </ol>

                    <p><strong>Example scenario (hypothetical):</strong></p>
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Recipient</th>
                                <th>% of Pot</th>
                                <th>Amount (1,000 coin pot)</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Platform fee</td>
                                <td>10%</td>
                                <td>100 coins</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Super Klasher host fee</td>
                                <td>5%</td>
                                <td>50 coins</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>1st place</td>
                                <td>50%</td>
                                <td>425 coins</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>2nd place</td>
                                <td>30%</td>
                                <td>255 coins</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>3rd place</td>
                                <td>20%</td>
                                <td>170 coins</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                    <p><em>Note: Percentages are illustrative only — actual values require Lincoln confirmation.</em></p>

                    <h5 class="mt-3">3. Subscription Revenue (If Applicable)</h5>
                    <p>If Independent/Super tiers require subscriptions:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Independent Klasher:</strong> £X/month (TBD)</li>
                        <li><strong>Super Klasher:</strong> £Y/month (TBD)</li>
                        <li><strong>App store commission:</strong> Apple/Google take 15-30% of subscriptions</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h4 class="mt-3">Upgrade Mechanisms (Undefined)</h4>
                    <p>How users move between tiers is <strong>not specified</strong> in source documents. Three possible models:</p>

                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Model</th>
                                <th>Klasher → Independent</th>
                                <th>Independent → Super</th>
                                <th>Pros</th>
                                <th>Cons</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>1. Achievement-Based</strong></td>
                                <td>Reach 1,000 followers + 1,000 wins</td>
                                <td>Reach 10,000 followers + 5,000 wins</td>
                                <td>Free, meritocratic, drives engagement</td>
                                <td>No direct revenue from upgrades</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>2. Payment-Based</strong></td>
                                <td>Pay £10/month subscription</td>
                                <td>Pay £50/month subscription</td>
                                <td>Predictable recurring revenue</td>
                                <td>Paywall may limit adoption</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>3. Application-Based</strong></td>
                                <td>Apply + manual approval</td>
                                <td>Apply + manual approval</td>
                                <td>Quality control, exclusivity</td>
                                <td>Manual overhead, slow upgrades</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>

                    <p class="mt-3"><strong>BRD Quote:</strong> "minimum 1000 followers AND 1000 wins to receive klash coins" — suggests achievement model for Klasher tier, but unclear if this applies to upgrades.</p>

                    <p class="mt-3"><strong>See full analysis:</strong> <a href="payment-tiers.html">Payment Plans & Tiers</a></p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- 2.6 Domain & Regulatory Requirements -->
            <section class="card" id="section-2-6">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <h3 class="card-title mb-0">2.6 Domain & Regulatory Requirements</h3>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p>KlashOut operates in heavily regulated domains: <strong>financial services</strong>, <strong>music licensing</strong>, <strong>data privacy</strong>, and <strong>app store distribution</strong>. These requirements are non-negotiable and carry legal/financial stakes.</p>

                    <h4>D01: Music Licensing & Copyright <span class="badge badge-blocked">BLOCKING</span></h4>
                    <p><strong>Requirement:</strong> All music uploaded to the platform must either:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Be original works owned by the uploader (Independent/Super Klashers), OR</li>
                        <li>Have appropriate licensing agreements if copyrighted material</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>Regulatory Bodies:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>UK:</strong> PRS for Music, PPL (Phonographic Performance Limited)</li>
                        <li><strong>US:</strong> ASCAP, BMI, SESAC</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>Risk:</strong> Copyright infringement lawsuits, platform takedown, criminal penalties</p>
                    <p><strong>Mitigation Strategy:</strong></p>
                    <ol>
                        <li><strong>Phase 1:</strong> User-uploaded content only (users certify they own rights)</li>
                        <li>Implement DMCA takedown process (Digital Millennium Copyright Act compliance)</li>
                        <li>Content ID system (detect copyrighted material — future phase)</li>
                        <li>Partner with licensing aggregator (e.g., SoundExchange) for Phase 2 expansion</li>
                    </ol>
                    <p><strong>Open Items:</strong> Q7.1 (licensing strategy), Q7.2 (DMCA process)</p>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h4 class="mt-3">D02: FCA E-Money Regulations (Financial Services) <span class="badge badge-completed">RESOLVED</span></h4>
                    <p><strong>Requirement:</strong> 1:1 fiat-backed virtual currency (Klash Coin) requires FCA compliance.</p>
                    <p><strong>Regulatory Framework:</strong> UK Electronic Money Regulations 2011</p>
                    <p><strong>Compliance Path (Recommended):</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Option 1:</strong> Partner with licensed e-money institution (Stripe Connect, Mangopay, Modulr)</li>
                        <li><strong>Option 2:</strong> Apply for Small E-Money Institution (SEMI) license (6-12 months, £5K+ legal costs)</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>Why Option 1 is recommended:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>✅ Faster to market (integrate in weeks vs months for license)</li>
                        <li>✅ Lower upfront cost (no application fees)</li>
                        <li>✅ FCA compliance inherited from partner</li>
                        <li>✅ Payment processing infrastructure included</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>Requirements for Partner Integration:</strong></p>
                    <ol>
                        <li>Know Your Customer (KYC) verification for users (ID upload)</li>
                        <li>Anti-Money Laundering (AML) monitoring</li>
                        <li>Transaction reporting to FCA</li>
                        <li>Safeguarding of customer funds (segregated accounts)</li>
                    </ol>
                    <p><strong>Decision:</strong> Use Stripe Connect or Mangopay (Lincoln to confirm preference)</p>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h4 class="mt-3">D03: GDPR Data Protection (Privacy) <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span></h4>
                    <p><strong>Requirement:</strong> Comply with General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) 2018 for UK/EU users.</p>
                    <p><strong>Key Obligations:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Lawful basis:</strong> User consent for data processing (registration flow)</li>
                        <li><strong>Right to access:</strong> Users can download all their data (export feature)</li>
                        <li><strong>Right to erasure:</strong> Users can delete accounts ("right to be forgotten")</li>
                        <li><strong>Data minimization:</strong> Collect only necessary data</li>
                        <li><strong>Breach notification:</strong> Report data breaches to ICO within 72 hours</li>
                        <li><strong>Privacy policy:</strong> Clear, accessible explanation of data usage</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>Technical Implementation:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Cookie consent banner (for web)</li>
                        <li>Account deletion endpoint (soft delete with 30-day grace period)</li>
                        <li>Data export API (JSON format)</li>
                        <li>Encryption at rest (database, file storage)</li>
                    </ul>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h4 class="mt-3">D04: Age Verification (18+ Platform) <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span></h4>
                    <p><strong>Requirement:</strong> Klash Coin transactions require users to be 18+ (financial services regulation).</p>
                    <p><strong>Verification Methods:</strong></p>
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Method</th>
                                <th>Accuracy</th>
                                <th>User Friction</th>
                                <th>Cost</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Self-declaration (birthdate input)</td>
                                <td>Low (easily bypassed)</td>
                                <td>Very low</td>
                                <td>Free</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Credit card verification</td>
                                <td>High (must own card)</td>
                                <td>Medium</td>
                                <td>Payment processor fees</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>ID document upload (KYC)</td>
                                <td>Very high</td>
                                <td>High</td>
                                <td>£0.10-0.50 per verification</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                    <p><strong>Recommended:</strong> Self-declaration for registration, ID upload required before first Klash Coin purchase (KYC at payment threshold).</p>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h4 class="mt-3">D05: App Store Guidelines <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span></h4>

                    <h5>Apple App Store</h5>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>In-App Purchases:</strong> All digital goods MUST use Apple IAP (30% commission first year, 15% after)</li>
                        <li><strong>Virtual Currency:</strong> Klash Coins may trigger IAP requirement (unclear — needs Apple review)</li>
                        <li><strong>Workaround:</strong> Allow coin purchases via web only (bypass IAP), app uses existing balance</li>
                        <li><strong>User-Generated Content:</strong> Moderation required (profanity filter, reporting system)</li>
                        <li><strong>Age Rating:</strong> 17+ (due to user-generated content and financial transactions)</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h5 class="mt-3">Google Play Store</h5>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Google Play Billing:</strong> Required for digital goods (15% commission <$1M revenue, 30% after)</li>
                        <li><strong>Same IAP concerns as Apple</strong></li>
                        <li><strong>Alternative Payment Methods:</strong> Google allows linking to external payment (unlike Apple)</li>
                    </ul>

                    <p><strong>Open Items:</strong> Q8.6 (pricing strategy to account for 15-30% commission)</p>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h4 class="mt-3">Compliance Summary Table</h4>
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Requirement</th>
                                <th>Regulatory Body</th>
                                <th>Penalty for Non-Compliance</th>
                                <th>Status</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>D01:</strong> Music Licensing</td>
                                <td>PRS, PPL, ASCAP</td>
                                <td>Copyright lawsuits, platform shutdown</td>
                                <td><span class="badge badge-blocked">REQUIRES STRATEGY</span></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>D02:</strong> E-Money / FCA</td>
                                <td>UK Financial Conduct Authority</td>
                                <td>Fines, criminal charges, shutdown</td>
                                <td><span class="badge badge-completed">PARTNER WITH STRIPE/MANGOPAY</span></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>D03:</strong> GDPR</td>
                                <td>ICO (UK), CNIL (France), etc.</td>
                                <td>Up to €20M or 4% global revenue</td>
                                <td><span class="badge badge-must-have">IMPLEMENTABLE</span></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>D04:</strong> Age Verification</td>
                                <td>FCA (financial), ICO (GDPR)</td>
                                <td>Fines, regulatory action</td>
                                <td><span class="badge badge-must-have">IMPLEMENTABLE</span></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>D05:</strong> App Store Guidelines</td>
                                <td>Apple, Google</td>
                                <td>App rejection, removal from store</td>
                                <td><span class="badge badge-should-have">REQUIRES PRICING STRATEGY</span></td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>

                    <p class="mt-3"><strong>Legal Review Recommended:</strong> Engage solicitor specializing in fintech/music licensing before Phase 2 implementation.</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- 3.0 DETAILED REQUIREMENTS SPECIFICATION -->
            <section class="card" id="section-3">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <h2 class="card-title mb-0">3.0 Detailed Requirements Specification</h2>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p class="alert alert-warning">This section describes the system from a <strong>developer-technical perspective</strong>. For stakeholder-friendly descriptions, see <a href="#section-2">Section 2</a>.</p>
                    <p>Section 3 provides precise, measurable, testable requirements for implementation teams. All requirements are traceable to source documents or explicitly flagged as working assumptions.</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- 3.1 External Interface Requirements -->
            <section class="card" id="section-3-1">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <h3 class="card-title mb-0">3.1 External Interface Requirements</h3>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p>This section defines all interfaces between KlashOut and external systems, services, and users.</p>

                    <h4>3.1.1 User Interfaces</h4>

                    <h5>Web Application (React)</h5>
                    <p><strong>Target Platforms:</strong> Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge (latest 2 versions)</p>
                    <p><strong>Screen Resolutions:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Desktop:</strong> 1920×1080 (primary), 1366×768 (minimum), 2560×1440 (supported)</li>
                        <li><strong>Mobile Web:</strong> 375×667 (iPhone SE), 414×896 (iPhone 11 Pro), 360×640 (Android common)</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>Responsive Breakpoints:</strong></p>
                    <pre><code>// Tailwind CSS / standard breakpoints
sm: 640px   // Small tablets, large phones (landscape)
md: 768px   // Tablets
lg: 1024px  // Small laptops
xl: 1280px  // Desktops
2xl: 1536px // Large desktops</code></pre>

                    <p><strong>Accessibility:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>WCAG 2.1 Level AA compliance</li>
                        <li>Keyboard navigation support (tab order, focus indicators)</li>
                        <li>Screen reader compatibility (ARIA labels)</li>
                        <li>Color contrast ratio ≥4.5:1 (text to background)</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h5 class="mt-3">Mobile Applications (React Native)</h5>
                    <p><strong>iOS:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Minimum version:</strong> iOS 14.0</li>
                        <li><strong>Devices:</strong> iPhone 8 and newer, iPad (5th gen) and newer</li>
                        <li><strong>Orientations:</strong> Portrait (primary), Landscape (supported for iPad)</li>
                        <li><strong>App Store requirements:</strong> 17+ age rating (UGC + financial transactions)</li>
                    </ul>

                    <p><strong>Android:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Minimum version:</strong> Android 8.0 (Oreo, API level 26)</li>
                        <li><strong>Target version:</strong> Android 13 (API level 33)</li>
                        <li><strong>Screen sizes:</strong> Small (320dp), Normal (360dp), Large (480dp), XLarge (720dp)</li>
                        <li><strong>Play Store requirements:</strong> PEGI 18 / ESRB Mature rating</li>
                    </ul>

                    <p><strong>UI Design System:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Typography:</strong> System font stack (SF Pro for iOS, Roboto for Android, Inter for Web)</li>
                        <li><strong>Color palette:</strong>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Primary (KO Blue): #00d4ff</li>
                                <li>Klasher tier: #0066cc (Blue)</li>
                                <li>Independent tier: #ffaa00 (Gold)</li>
                                <li>Super Klasher tier: #ff0080 (Pink)</li>
                                <li>Background: #0a0e1a (Dark theme primary)</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li><strong>Icons:</strong> React Native Vector Icons (Material Icons, Ionicons)</li>
                    </ul>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h4 class="mt-3">3.1.2 API Interfaces</h4>

                    <h5>Backend API (RESTful + WebSockets)</h5>
                    <p><strong>Base URL:</strong> <code>https://api.klashout.com/v1</code></p>
                    <p><strong>Authentication:</strong> JWT Bearer tokens in Authorization header</p>
                    <pre><code>Authorization: Bearer {jwt_token}</code></pre>

                    <p><strong>API Structure:</strong></p>
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Resource</th>
                                <th>Endpoints</th>
                                <th>Methods</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>/auth</strong></td>
                                <td>/register, /login, /refresh, /logout</td>
                                <td>POST</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>/users</strong></td>
                                <td>/users/{id}, /users/{id}/profile, /users/{id}/stats</td>
                                <td>GET, PUT, DELETE</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>/tracks</strong></td>
                                <td>/tracks, /tracks/{id}, /tracks/upload</td>
                                <td>GET, POST, PUT, DELETE</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>/klashes</strong></td>
                                <td>/klashes, /klashes/{id}, /klashes/{id}/vote</td>
                                <td>GET, POST, PUT</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>/wallet</strong></td>
                                <td>/wallet/balance, /wallet/topup, /wallet/transactions</td>
                                <td>GET, POST</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>/tournaments</strong></td>
                                <td>/tournaments, /tournaments/{id}, /tournaments/{id}/enter</td>
                                <td>GET, POST</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>

                    <p><strong>Request/Response Format:</strong> JSON</p>
                    <pre><code>// Example: GET /klashes/{id}
{
  "id": "uuid-v4",
  "genre": "reggae",
  "duration": 60,
  "status": "in_progress",
  "participants": [
    {
      "user_id": "uuid",
      "klasher_name": "DJSoundWave",
      "track_id": "uuid",
      "votes": 42
    }
  ],
  "start_time": "2026-07-24T14:30:00Z"
}</code></pre>

                    <p><strong>Error Handling:</strong> Standard HTTP status codes + error object</p>
                    <pre><code>// Error response format
{
  "error": {
    "code": "INVALID_CREDENTIALS",
    "message": "Email or password is incorrect",
    "status": 401
  }
}</code></pre>

                    <h5 class="mt-3">WebSocket Interface (Real-Time Events)</h5>
                    <p><strong>Endpoint:</strong> <code>wss://ws.klashout.com</code></p>
                    <p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Real-time klash state updates, voting, chat</p>

                    <p><strong>Connection Flow:</strong></p>
                    <ol>
                        <li>Client establishes WebSocket connection with JWT token: <code>wss://ws.klashout.com?token={jwt}</code></li>
                        <li>Server authenticates and sends <code>{"type": "connected"}</code></li>
                        <li>Client subscribes to klash: <code>{"type": "subscribe", "klash_id": "uuid"}</code></li>
                        <li>Server broadcasts events: <code>{"type": "vote", "user_id": "...", "votes": 43}</code></li>
                    </ol>

                    <p><strong>Event Types:</strong></p>
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Event</th>
                                <th>Direction</th>
                                <th>Payload</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td><code>vote</code></td>
                                <td>Client → Server</td>
                                <td><code>{"klash_id": "...", "participant_id": "..."}</code></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><code>vote_update</code></td>
                                <td>Server → Clients</td>
                                <td><code>{"participant_id": "...", "votes": 45}</code></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><code>klash_start</code></td>
                                <td>Server → Clients</td>
                                <td><code>{"klash_id": "...", "start_time": "..."}</code></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><code>klash_end</code></td>
                                <td>Server → Clients</td>
                                <td><code>{"klash_id": "...", "winner_id": "...", "result": {...}}</code></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><code>chat_message</code></td>
                                <td>Bidirectional</td>
                                <td><code>{"user_id": "...", "message": "...", "timestamp": "..."}</code></td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>

                    <p><strong>Performance Requirement:</strong> Event delivery latency ≤200ms (p95) — see NF02</p>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h4 class="mt-3">3.1.3 Payment Provider Interface</h4>

                    <h5>Stripe Connect Integration</h5>
                    <p><strong>Purpose:</strong> FCA-compliant e-money handling, card processing, payouts</p>
                    <p><strong>API:</strong> Stripe REST API v2023-10-16 (or latest)</p>

                    <p><strong>Required Stripe Products:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Payment Intents API:</strong> Top-up transactions (credit/debit card)</li>
                        <li><strong>Payouts API:</strong> Cash-out to bank account</li>
                        <li><strong>Connect:</strong> Split payments (Super Klash hosting fees)</li>
                        <li><strong>Identity:</strong> KYC verification for 18+ age check</li>
                    </ul>

                    <p><strong>Webhook Events:</strong></p>
                    <pre><code>// Endpoint: POST /api/webhooks/stripe
// Events to subscribe to:
payment_intent.succeeded
payment_intent.failed
payout.paid
payout.failed
identity.verification_session.verified
identity.verification_session.requires_input</code></pre>

                    <p><strong>Idempotency:</strong> All payment requests must include <code>Idempotency-Key</code> header to prevent double-charging</p>

                    <p><strong>Alternative: Mangopay</strong> (if Stripe Connect unavailable)</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Similar FCA compliance via e-money license</li>
                        <li>REST API v2.01</li>
                        <li>Marketplace features for split payments</li>
                    </ul>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h4 class="mt-3">3.1.4 File Storage Interface</h4>

                    <h5>Cloudflare R2 (S3-Compatible)</h5>
                    <p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Music file storage, profile images, static assets</p>
                    <p><strong>API:</strong> AWS S3 API (compatible)</p>

                    <p><strong>Bucket Structure:</strong></p>
                    <pre><code>klashout-music/
  ├── tracks/{user_id}/{track_id}.mp3
  ├── tracks/{user_id}/{track_id}.wav
  └── tracks/{user_id}/{track_id}.flac

klashout-images/
  ├── profiles/{user_id}/avatar.jpg
  └── covers/{track_id}/cover.jpg</code></pre>

                    <p><strong>Upload Flow:</strong></p>
                    <ol>
                        <li>Client requests pre-signed upload URL: <code>POST /api/tracks/upload-url</code></li>
                        <li>Server generates R2 pre-signed URL (expires in 15 minutes)</li>
                        <li>Client uploads directly to R2 using pre-signed URL</li>
                        <li>Client confirms upload: <code>POST /api/tracks</code> with file metadata</li>
                    </ol>

                    <p><strong>CDN Delivery:</strong> Cloudflare CDN (automatic with R2)</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Public URL format:</strong> <code>https://cdn.klashout.com/tracks/{track_id}.mp3</code></li>
                        <li><strong>Cache control:</strong> <code>Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000</code> (1 year for immutable files)</li>
                        <li><strong>Streaming:</strong> Range request support for progressive audio playback</li>
                    </ul>

                    <p><strong>File Processing Pipeline:</strong></p>
                    <ol>
                        <li>Upload received → Virus scan (ClamAV or equivalent)</li>
                        <li>Format validation (ffprobe to detect MP3/WAV/FLAC)</li>
                        <li>Transcoding (if needed): Convert to 320kbps MP3 for web streaming</li>
                        <li>Metadata extraction (duration, BPM, artist, title)</li>
                        <li>Generate waveform visualization (optional)</li>
                    </ol>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h4 class="mt-3">3.1.5 Third-Party Services</h4>

                    <h5>Email Service (Transactional)</h5>
                    <p><strong>Provider:</strong> SendGrid or Amazon SES</p>
                    <p><strong>Use Cases:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Registration confirmation (verify email)</li>
                        <li>Password reset</li>
                        <li>Klash invitations (direct challenge)</li>
                        <li>Tournament notifications</li>
                        <li>Transaction receipts (top-up, cash-out)</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>Template Format:</strong> Handlebars or Mustache templates with HTML + plain text fallback</p>

                    <h5 class="mt-3">SMS Service (2FA / Notifications)</h5>
                    <p><strong>Provider:</strong> Twilio or AWS SNS</p>
                    <p><strong>Use Cases:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Two-factor authentication (optional)</li>
                        <li>Cash-out verification code</li>
                        <li>High-value transaction alerts</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h5 class="mt-3">Analytics & Monitoring</h5>
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Service</th>
                                <th>Purpose</th>
                                <th>Integration</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Google Analytics 4</strong></td>
                                <td>User behavior tracking, conversion funnels</td>
                                <td>JavaScript SDK (web), Firebase Analytics (mobile)</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Sentry</strong></td>
                                <td>Error tracking, performance monitoring</td>
                                <td>Sentry SDK (Node.js, React, React Native)</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Datadog / Grafana</strong></td>
                                <td>Infrastructure monitoring, logs, APM</td>
                                <td>StatsD / Prometheus metrics</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>

                    <h5 class="mt-3">Push Notifications</h5>
                    <p><strong>iOS:</strong> Apple Push Notification Service (APNs)</p>
                    <p><strong>Android:</strong> Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM)</p>
                    <p><strong>Use Cases:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Klash invitation received</li>
                        <li>Tournament starting soon</li>
                        <li>You won a klash!</li>
                        <li>Someone followed you</li>
                        <li>New message received</li>
                    </ul>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h4 class="mt-3">3.1.6 Hardware Interfaces</h4>
                    <p><strong>Audio Playback:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Web:</strong> HTML5 Audio API / Web Audio API</li>
                        <li><strong>iOS:</strong> AVFoundation (AVAudioPlayer)</li>
                        <li><strong>Android:</strong> MediaPlayer API / ExoPlayer</li>
                    </ul>

                    <p><strong>Microphone Access:</strong> Not required for Phase 1 (Go Live video feature deferred)</p>

                    <p><strong>Camera Access:</strong> Profile photo upload only (iOS/Android native photo picker)</p>

                    <hr class="mt-3">

                    <h4 class="mt-3">3.1.7 Communication Protocols</h4>
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Protocol</th>
                                <th>Use Case</th>
                                <th>Port</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>HTTPS (TLS 1.3)</strong></td>
                                <td>All REST API requests</td>
                                <td>443</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>WSS (WebSocket Secure)</strong></td>
                                <td>Real-time klash events</td>
                                <td>443</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>PostgreSQL Wire Protocol</strong></td>
                                <td>Backend ↔ Database</td>
                                <td>5432 (internal)</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Redis Protocol (RESP)</strong></td>
                                <td>Backend ↔ Cache/Pub-Sub</td>
                                <td>6379 (internal)</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>

                    <p class="mt-3"><strong>Security Requirements:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>All public-facing traffic MUST use TLS 1.3 (TLS 1.2 minimum)</li>
                        <li>Certificate validation enforced (no self-signed certs in production)</li>
                        <li>HSTS header: <code>Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains</code></li>
                        <li>CORS policy: Whitelist only <code>klashout.com</code>, <code>*.klashout.com</code></li>
                    </ul>

                    <p class="mt-3"><strong>See Also:</strong> <a href="system-design.html">System Design Document</a> for complete API specification and sequence diagrams.</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- 3.2 Functional Requirements (User Stories) -->
            <section class="card" id="section-3-2">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <h3 class="card-title mb-0">3.2 Functional Requirements (User Stories)</h3>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p>This section specifies all functional requirements using the <strong>user story format</strong> with detailed acceptance criteria. Requirements are organized by epic and presented in the format:</p>

                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Requirement ID</strong> (F##) — Unique identifier used across all project documents</li>
                        <li><strong>User Story</strong> — "As a [role], I want [feature], so that [benefit]"</li>
                        <li><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong> — Testable conditions in Given/When/Then (Gherkin) format</li>
                        <li><strong>Priority (MoSCoW)</strong> — Must Have / Should Have / Could Have / Won't Have</li>
                        <li><strong>Weight</strong> — Estimated complexity (S/M/L/XL)</li>
                        <li><strong>Dependencies</strong> — Other requirements that must be implemented first</li>
                    </ul>

                    <p><strong>Total Functional Requirements:</strong> 71 user stories (F01-F71)</p>
                    <p><strong>Priority Breakdown:</strong> 44 Must Have • 20 Should Have • 6 Could Have • 1 Won't Have</p>

                    <div class="alert alert-warning mt-3">
                        <div class="alert-title">⚠️ Open Items Flag</div>
                        <p>18 user stories have unresolved dependencies or undefined parameters requiring Lincoln's input. These are flagged with <strong>Open Item</strong> annotations. See <a href="questions-for-lincoln.html">Questions for Lincoln</a> and <a href="conflicts.html">Conflict Register</a> for complete list.</p>
                    </div>

                    <hr class="mt-4 mb-4">

                    <!-- Epic 1: User Account Management -->
                    <h4 id="epic-1-stories">Epic 1: User Account Management</h4>
                    <p class="text-muted">Foundation epic — authentication, authorization, tier system, privacy. Must build first.</p>

                    <!-- F01 -->
                    <div class="card mt-3">
                        <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                            <h5 class="mb-0">F01 — User Registration with Unique Username <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: S</span></h5>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                            As a user, I want to create an account with a unique username so that I can be identified on the platform.</p>

                            <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                            <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Successful account registration with unique username
Given a new user is on the registration screen
When they submit a username that does not already exist on the platform
Then the system shall create the account and redirect the user to their new profile

Scenario: Registration attempt with duplicate username
Given a new user is on the registration screen
When they submit a username that already exists on the platform
Then the system shall reject the submission and display an error message stating the username is taken
And the system shall not create a new account</code></pre>

                            <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> None</p>
                            <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- F02 -->
                    <div class="card mt-3">
                        <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                            <h5 class="mb-0">F02 — Password-Protected Account Access <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: S</span></h5>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                            As a user, I want my account to be password protected so that my account is secure and only I can access it.</p>

                            <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                            <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Successful login with valid credentials
Given a registered user is on the login screen
When they enter their correct email and password
Then the system shall authenticate the user and grant access to their account

Scenario: Failed login with incorrect credentials
Given a registered user is on the login screen
When they enter an incorrect email or password
Then the system shall reject the login attempt and display a generic error message
And the error message shall not reveal which specific field (email or password) is incorrect
And the account shall not be accessed

Scenario: Password minimum security requirement
Given a new user is on the registration screen
When they submit a password shorter than 8 characters
Then the system shall reject the submission and display a password requirement error</code></pre>

                            <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> None</p>
                            <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>
                            <p><strong>Security Note:</strong> See Section 3.1.7 for authentication protocol requirements (JWT, TLS 1.3, bcrypt).</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- F03 -->
                    <div class="card mt-3">
                        <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                            <h5 class="mb-0">F03 — Privacy Settings Configuration <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                            As a user, I want to configure privacy settings on my account so that I can control what other users can see.</p>

                            <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                            <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: User sets profile to private
Given a logged-in user is in their account settings
When they toggle their profile to Private
Then the system shall hide their stats, klash history, and playlists from all users who do not follow them
And their profile shall display a private indicator to non-followers

Scenario: User sets profile to public
Given a logged-in user is in their account settings
When they toggle their profile to Public
Then all profile content shall be visible to any KO user</code></pre>

                            <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F01</p>
                            <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>
                            <p><strong>Regulatory Note:</strong> Privacy controls are required for D04 (UK GDPR) compliance. See <a href="#section-2-6">Section 2.6</a>.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- F04 -->
                    <div class="card mt-3">
                        <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                            <h5 class="mb-0">F04 — Klasher Tier Assignment & Access Control <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: L</span></h5>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                            As a user, I want to be assigned a Klasher tier so that I have access to the features appropriate to my level.</p>

                            <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                            <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Tier displayed on profile
Given a user has an active account with an assigned tier
When any user views that profile
Then the tier (Klasher, Independent Klasher, or Super Klasher) shall be displayed visibly on the profile

Scenario: Tier-gated feature access for Independent Klasher
Given a user with a standard Klasher tier attempts to access an Independent Klasher feature (e.g. uploading music)
When they attempt to access that feature
Then the system shall restrict access and display an appropriate upgrade prompt

Scenario: Tier-gated feature access for Super Klasher
Given a user with a standard Klasher tier attempts to access a Super Klasher feature (e.g. setting stakes)
When they attempt to access that feature
Then the system shall restrict access accordingly</code></pre>

                            <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F01</p>
                            <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>

                            <div class="alert alert-warning">
                                <strong>⚠️ Open Item Q1.1:</strong> The process for upgrading between tiers (how a user becomes an Independent Klasher or Super Klasher) is not yet defined. Clarify with Lincoln:
                                <ul class="mb-0">
                                    <li>Is tier upgrade manual (admin approval) or automated (payment-gated)?</li>
                                    <li>What are the verification requirements for Independent Klasher (rights ownership proof)?</li>
                                    <li>What are the eligibility criteria for Super Klasher?</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <p class="mt-3"><strong>Epic 1 Summary:</strong> 4 user stories • All Must Have • Builds User entity, authentication, RBAC tier system</p>

                    <hr class="mt-4 mb-4">

                    <!-- Epic 2: Music Library & Song Selection -->
                    <h4 id="epic-2-stories" class="mt-4">Epic 2: Music Library & Song Selection</h4>
                    <p class="text-muted">Content layer — music storage, streaming, upload, browse. No music = no klashes.</p>

                    <!-- F05 -->
                    <div class="card mt-3">
                        <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                            <h5 class="mb-0">F05 — Song Selection from KO Library for Klash <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                            As a user, I want to select a song from the KO library to use in a klash so that I can compete using music I like.</p>

                            <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                            <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: User browses and selects a track for a klash
Given a logged-in user is in the klash setup flow
When they open the song selection screen
Then the system shall display the KO library with search and browse functionality
And when the user selects a track, it shall be queued for the klash session
And the user shall be shown a confirmation of their selection before the klash begins

Scenario: User searches for a specific track
Given a user is on the song selection screen
When they enter a search term
Then the system shall return relevant tracks from the KO library matching the search term</code></pre>

                            <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F01</p>
                            <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>
                            <p><strong>Design Note:</strong> Search implementation details in Section 3.1.2 (API /tracks endpoint).</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- F06 -->
                    <div class="card mt-3">
                        <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                            <h5 class="mb-0">F06 — Add Song to Playlist <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: S</span></h5>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                            As a user, I want to select a song from the KO library to add to a playlist so that I can save music I enjoy.</p>

                            <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                            <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: User adds a track to an existing playlist
Given a user is browsing the KO library
When they select "Add to Playlist" on a track and choose an existing playlist
Then the system shall add the track to that playlist and display a confirmation message

Scenario: User attempts to add a duplicate track
Given a user attempts to add a track already in their playlist
When they confirm the addition
Then the system shall flag the duplicate and prompt the user to confirm whether to add it again</code></pre>

                            <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F05, F22 (Playlist CRUD)</p>
                            <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- F07 -->
                    <div class="card mt-3">
                        <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                            <h5 class="mb-0">F07 — Music Upload (Independent Klasher) <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: L</span></h5>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                            As an Independent Klasher, I want to upload my own music to the platform so that I can klash with and promote my own tracks.</p>

                            <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                            <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Successful music upload
Given a logged-in Independent Klasher is on the upload screen
When they submit a music file in a supported format
Then the system shall display an upload progress indicator
And upon completion the track shall appear in the user's private library
And the track shall be available for use in klashes

Scenario: Upload by non-Independent Klasher
Given a logged-in standard Klasher attempts to access the upload feature
When they navigate to the upload screen
Then the system shall restrict access and display a tier upgrade prompt

Scenario: Unsupported file format
Given a user attempts to upload a file in an unsupported format
When they submit the file
Then the system shall reject the upload and display an error specifying supported formats</code></pre>

                            <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F04 (Tier system)</p>
                            <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>

                            <div class="alert alert-warning">
                                <strong>⚠️ Open Item Q2.3:</strong> Define technical parameters for music upload:
                                <ul class="mb-0">
                                    <li>Supported file formats (MP3, WAV, FLAC, AAC?)</li>
                                    <li>Maximum file size limit</li>
                                    <li>Rights declaration mechanism (checkbox? legal statement?)</li>
                                    <li>Upload quota per Independent Klasher (unlimited or capped?)</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>

                            <p><strong>Regulatory Note:</strong> D01 (Music Licensing) — uploads require rights verification before making tracks publicly available.</p>
                            <p><strong>Technical Note:</strong> Upload flow uses Cloudflare R2 with direct upload. See Section 3.1.4 for file storage interface specs.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- F08 -->
                    <div class="card mt-3">
                        <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                            <h5 class="mb-0">F08 — Track Download (Owner-Enabled) <span class="badge badge-could-have">COULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                            As a user, I want to download a track where the owner has enabled downloads so that I can listen offline.</p>

                            <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                            <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Download-enabled track
Given a user is viewing a track where the owner has enabled downloads
When they tap the download button
Then the system shall download the file to the user's device and confirm completion

Scenario: Download-disabled track
Given a user is viewing a track where downloads are not enabled
When they view the track options
Then the system shall not display a download button for that track</code></pre>

                            <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F07 (Upload must exist for ownership concept)</p>
                            <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <p class="mt-3"><strong>Epic 2 Summary:</strong> 4 user stories • 2 Must Have, 1 Should Have, 1 Could Have • Builds Track entity, S3 storage, CDN streaming</p>

                    <hr class="mt-4 mb-4">

                    <!-- Epic 3: Klashing (Core Game Loop) -->
        <!-- Epic 3: Klashing - Core Game -->
        <h4 id="epic-3-stories" class="mt-4">Epic 3: Klashing — Core Game Loop</h4>
        <p class="text-muted">The core competitive game loop that defines KlashOut: direct challenges, matchmaking, song selection, voting, scoring, and result determination.</p>

        <!-- F09 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F09 — Direct Klash Request <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Klasher, I want to request a klash with another KO user so that I can compete against them directly.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Klash request sent
Given a logged-in Klasher is viewing another user's profile
When they tap the Klash Request button
Then the system shall send a klash request notification to the recipient

Scenario: Klash request accepted
Given a user has received a klash request notification
When they accept the request
Then the system shall initiate the klash setup flow for both users

Scenario: Klash request declined
Given a user has received a klash request notification
When they decline the request
Then the system shall notify the requester that the request was declined
And no klash shall commence</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F01, F04</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F10 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F10 — Klash Duration Selection <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: S</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Klasher, I want to set the duration of my klash (30, 60, or 90 seconds) so that I can control the format of the game.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Duration selection in direct klash
Given a Klasher is in the klash setup flow
When they are presented with the duration selection screen
Then the system shall display three options: 30 seconds, 60 seconds, and 90 seconds
And the selected duration shall apply to both participants for the entirety of the klash
And the user shall not be able to proceed without selecting a duration</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F09</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F11 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F11 — Group Klash with Participant Cap (50 Users) <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: L</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Klasher, I want to invite up to 50 participants to my klash so that I can host a group competition.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Group klash invitation within cap
Given a Klasher is setting up a group klash
When they send invitations and the total number of accepted participants is 50 or fewer
Then the system shall permit all participants to join

Scenario: Group klash exceeds participant cap
Given a Klasher is setting up a group klash and 50 participants have already accepted
When an additional user attempts to join
Then the system shall prevent the additional user from joining and display a "klash full" message</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F09, F04</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F12 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F12 — Super Klasher Unlimited Participant Klash <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: XL</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Super Klasher, I want to host klashes with an unlimited number of participants so that I can run large-scale events.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Super Klasher hosts a large klash
Given a logged-in Super Klasher is setting up a klash
When participants join
Then the system shall enforce no upper participant cap for Super Klasher-organised klashes
And the system shall scale to support the number of concurrent participants</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F04</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>

                <p><strong>Technical Note:</strong> "Unlimited" must be scoped practically — the system needs a technically defined maximum (e.g. 10,000 concurrent users) even if not presented to the user. Confirm infrastructure expectations with Lincoln.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F13 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F13 — Super Klasher Staking & Entry Fees <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Super Klasher, I want to set the stakes for each klash I host so that I can define what participants are competing for.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Super Klasher sets entry stakes
Given a Super Klasher is configuring a klash
When they set a joining fee amount
Then the system shall display the stakes clearly on the klash listing
And all participants shall see and confirm the entry cost before joining
And the entry fee shall be debited from each participant's Klash Coin wallet upon joining</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F04, F46</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F14 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F14 — Scoring System: Win/Loss/Draw Record <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a user, I want a scoring system to record my klash results so that I can track my wins, losses, and draws.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Win recorded
Given a klash has concluded and a winner has been determined
When the result is confirmed by the system
Then a win shall be added to the winner's record immediately
And a loss shall be added to the loser's record immediately

Scenario: Draw recorded
Given a klash has concluded with a tied vote
When the result is confirmed
Then a draw shall be added to both participants' records</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F41</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F15 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F15 — Klash History Viewing <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a user, I want to view my previous klashes so that I can review my performance history.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: User views klash history
Given a logged-in user navigates to their klash history
When the history screen loads
Then the system shall display a list of past klashes in reverse chronological order
And each entry shall show: date, result (W/L/D), opponent name, and track used</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F14</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F16 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F16 — Klash Pinning to Profile (24-Hour Window) <span class="badge badge-could-have">COULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a user, I want to add a completed klash to my profile page within 24 hours so that I can showcase it to other users.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: User pins a klash within 24 hours
Given a klash has just ended
When the user selects "Add to Profile" within 24 hours of the klash ending
Then the klash shall be pinned to their profile page and visible to other users

Scenario: Option expires after 24 hours
Given a klash ended more than 24 hours ago
When the user views that klash in their history
Then the "Add to Profile" option shall no longer be available for that klash
And the klash shall remain in history but shall not be pinnable</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F15</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F30 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F30 — Klash Space Selection by Genre <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Klasher, I want to go online and enter a klash space based on music genre so that I am matched with klashers who share similar music taste.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Klasher selects a klash space
Given a logged-in Klasher taps "Go Online"
When the klash space selection screen appears
Then the system shall display a list of available genre-based klash spaces (e.g. Hip-Hop, Rock, Afrobeats)
And the user shall select exactly one space before proceeding
And the system shall not allow matchmaking to begin until a space is selected</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F01, F04</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Lincoln Interview</p>

                <div class="alert alert-warning">
                    <strong>⚠️ Open Item Q10:</strong> The definitive list of klash spaces (genres) to be confirmed with Lincoln.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F31 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F31 — Game Type Selection by Snippet Duration <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: S</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Klasher, I want to select a game type based on snippet duration so that I can compete in a format that suits me.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Duration selected after genre
Given a Klasher has selected a klash space
When they proceed to the duration selection screen
Then the system shall present three options: 30 seconds, 60 seconds, 90 seconds
And the selected duration shall apply to both klashers in the match
And the user shall not be able to proceed to matchmaking without a selection</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F30</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Lincoln Interview</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F32 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F32 — Automated Matchmaking with Queue Management <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: XL</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Klasher, I want to be automatically matched with another online Klasher who has selected similar settings so that my opponent is a relevant match.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Match found
Given a Klasher has confirmed their genre and duration settings
When another online Klasher with matching settings is available in the queue
Then the system shall pair both klashers and proceed to the pre-klash confirmation screen

Scenario: No match available — waiting state
Given a Klasher has confirmed their settings
When no matching opponent is currently available
Then the system shall display a waiting state with a visual indicator
And continue searching until a match is found or a timeout occurs

Scenario: Matchmaking timeout
Given a Klasher has been waiting for a match beyond the timeout period (duration TBD with Lincoln)
When the timeout expires
Then the system shall notify the user that no match was found and offer options to retry or exit</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F30, F31</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Lincoln Interview</p>

                <div class="alert alert-warning">
                    <strong>⚠️ Open Item Q11:</strong> Matchmaking timeout duration and behaviour to be confirmed with Lincoln.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F33 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F33 — Match Found Notification & Confirmation <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Klasher, I want to be notified when a match has been found so that I know the klash is about to begin.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Match found notification
Given the matchmaking system has paired two klashers
When the match is confirmed
Then both klashers shall receive a match notification showing the opponent's Klasher name
And both shall be prompted to confirm they are ready before the klash proceeds
And if either player does not confirm within a defined window, the match shall be cancelled (timeout TBD)</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F32</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Lincoln Interview</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F34 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F34 — Song Selection Before Klash Begins <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Klasher, I want to queue my song snippet choice before the klash begins so that I am prepared when it is my turn.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Klasher queues a song
Given both klashers have confirmed the match
When the song selection screen appears
Then each Klasher shall independently select a track from their library or the KO library
And the selection shall be confirmed before the countdown begins
And neither Klasher shall be able to see the other's selection at this stage</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F05, F23, F33</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Lincoln Interview</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F35 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F35 — Second Player Decision Window with Song Switch Option <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: L</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As the second Klasher, I want to hear my opponent's snippet before deciding whether to keep my queued song or switch so that I can make a strategic response.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Second Klasher hears first snippet and keeps original choice
Given the first Klasher's snippet has finished playing
When the second Klasher is presented with the decision window
And they choose to keep their originally queued song
Then their original selection shall play as their response

Scenario: Second Klasher switches song after hearing opponent
Given the first Klasher's snippet has finished playing
When the second Klasher selects a different track within the decision window
Then the new selection shall replace the original and play as their response

Scenario: Decision window expires with no action
Given the second Klasher has not made a selection within the decision window
When the window expires
Then the system shall automatically play the originally queued song</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F34</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Lincoln Interview</p>

                <p><strong>Technical Note:</strong> Duration of the decision window to be confirmed with Lincoln.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F36 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F36 — Countdown Timer Before Playback <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Klasher, I want a countdown to begin once both players have queued their songs so that the klash starts in a clear, structured way.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Countdown starts
Given both klashers have confirmed their song selections
When the system triggers the countdown
Then a visible countdown timer shall be displayed to both klashers and all spectators simultaneously
And the countdown duration shall be consistent (duration TBD with Lincoln)
And no further song changes shall be permitted once the countdown begins</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F34</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Lincoln Interview</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F37 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F37 — Random First-Player Selection <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: S</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Klasher, I want one player to be randomly selected to go first so that the game is fair.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Random first-player selection
Given the countdown has completed
When the klash is about to begin
Then the system shall randomly designate one Klasher as the first player and one as the second
And both players shall be notified of their position before playback begins
And the first player's snippet shall play immediately after notification</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F36</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Lincoln Interview</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F38 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F38 — Spectator Participation in Live Klash <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: L</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As an audience member, I want to listen to both song snippets during a klash so that I can follow the competition.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Spectator joins a live klash
Given a klash is in progress
When a spectator joins the klash as an audience member
Then the spectator shall see the current state of the klash
And shall hear whichever snippet is currently playing
And shall see both Klasher names and the current phase of the game (e.g. Player 1 playing, Player 2 responding, Voting)</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F37</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Lincoln Interview</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F39 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F39 — Live Klash Chat for Klashers and Spectators <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Klasher, I want to send messages in a live chat during the klash so that I can trash-talk my opponent and engage with the audience.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Klasher sends a chat message during klash
Given a klash is in progress
When a Klasher types and sends a message in the chat
Then the message shall appear in the chat window in real time for both klashers and all spectators

Scenario: Spectator views chat
Given a spectator is watching a live klash
When klashers are sending messages
Then all messages shall be visible to the spectator in real time</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F21, F33</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Lincoln Interview</p>

                <div class="alert alert-warning">
                    <strong>⚠️ Open Item Q17:</strong> Character limit per message, moderation policy, and whether spectators can also send messages to be confirmed with Lincoln.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F40 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F40 — Audience Voting After Klash <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: L</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As an audience member, I want to vote for my preferred snippet after both have played so that I can influence who wins the klash.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Audience member casts a vote
Given both snippets have finished playing
When the voting window opens
Then the system shall display the voting mechanism (likes / points — TBD) to all audience members
And each audience member shall be permitted to vote exactly once
And votes shall be tallied and displayed in real time

Scenario: Voting window closes
Given the voting window has been open for the defined duration (TBD with Lincoln)
When the window closes
Then the system shall lock all further votes and calculate the final result</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F38</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Lincoln Interview</p>

                <div class="alert alert-warning">
                    <strong>⚠️ Open Item Q5:</strong> Voting mechanism (like-based vs points allocation), voting window duration, and minimum audience size required for a valid result to be confirmed with Lincoln.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F41 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F41 — Winner Determination by Audience Vote <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: L</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Klasher, I want the winner to be determined by the audience vote or game point system so that the result feels community-driven and fair.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Winner determined by majority vote
Given the voting window has closed
When the system calculates the result
Then the Klasher with the most votes shall be declared the winner
And the result (win/loss/draw) shall be displayed clearly to both klashers and all spectators
And the result shall be recorded against both Klashers' profiles

Scenario: Draw declared
Given the voting window has closed with equal votes for both klashers
When the system calculates the result
Then a draw shall be declared and displayed to both parties</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F40</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Lincoln Interview</p>

                <p><strong>Technical Note:</strong> The exact scoring mechanism (pure vote count vs weighted points) to be confirmed with Lincoln.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F42 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F42 — Points Credit on Win <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Klasher, I want my points to increase when I win a klash so that my profile reflects my performance.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Points credited on win
Given a klash result has been confirmed as a win
When the result is processed
Then the winning Klasher's total points shall be incremented immediately
And the updated points total shall be visible on their profile</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F41, F14</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Lincoln Interview</p>

                <div class="alert alert-warning">
                    <strong>⚠️ Open Item Q7:</strong> Points value per win to be confirmed with Lincoln.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F43 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F43 — Points Deduction on Loss <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Klasher, I want my points to decrease when I lose a klash so that the scoring system reflects genuine competition.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Points deducted on loss
Given a klash result has been confirmed as a loss
When the result is processed
Then the losing Klasher's total points shall be decremented immediately
And the updated total shall be visible on their profile

Scenario: Points floor
Given a Klasher's current points total is at the minimum value (floor TBD with Lincoln)
When they lose a klash
Then the system shall not decrement their points below the defined floor value</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F41, F14</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Lincoln Interview</p>

                <div class="alert alert-warning">
                    <strong>⚠️ Open Item Q7, Q8:</strong> Points deduction value per loss and minimum points floor to be confirmed with Lincoln.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F44 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F44 — Public Stats Display on Profile <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Klasher, I want my wins, losses, draws, and total points to be visible on my profile so that other users can see my track record.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Stats displayed on public profile
Given a Klasher has a public profile
When any user views that profile
Then the system shall display: total klashes played, total wins, total losses, total draws, and total points
And all stats shall update in real time following each klash result</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F17, F42, F43</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Lincoln Interview</p>

                <p><strong>Technical Note:</strong> Whether stats are visible on private profiles to be confirmed with Lincoln.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F45 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F45 — Post-Klash Exit or Spectator Transition <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a losing Klasher, I want the option to exit or become a spectator after losing so that I can choose how to continue my session.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Loser chooses to exit
Given a Klasher has just lost a klash
When the result screen is shown and they select Exit
Then the system shall return them to their profile or the KO home screen

Scenario: Loser chooses to spectate
Given a Klasher has just lost a klash
When the result screen is shown and they select Spectate
Then the system shall transition them to spectator mode for the next available klash</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F41</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Lincoln Interview</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-3"><strong>Epic 3 Summary:</strong> 23 user stories • 15 Must Have, 6 Should Have, 2 Could Have • Builds the complete klashing game loop from matchmaking through voting to result determination</p>
        <hr class="mt-4 mb-4">

        <!-- Epic 4: Tournament Formats -->
        <h4 id="epic-4-stories" class="mt-4">Epic 4: Tournament Formats</h4>
        <p class="text-muted">Structured multi-round competition formats including Round Robin, Swiss System, Single Elimination, and Free-For-All.</p>

        <!-- F58 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F58 — Round Robin Tournament <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: XL</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Klasher, I want to enter a Round Robin tournament so that I can compete against every other participant at least once.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Round Robin pairing
Given a Round Robin tournament has started with N participants
When the system generates the schedule
Then every Klasher shall be paired against every other Klasher exactly once (single round robin)
And no player shall be eliminated after a loss

Scenario: Winner determination
Given all Round Robin matches have been completed
When the system calculates the final standings
Then the Klasher with the best win-loss record shall be declared the tournament winner
And in the event of a tie, a tiebreaker rule (to be defined with Lincoln) shall apply</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F32, F33</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Gaming Doc</p>

                <p><strong>Technical Note:</strong> Round Robin becomes operationally difficult with large groups (e.g. 50 players = 1,225 individual matches). A participant cap for this format should be defined.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F59 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F59 — Swiss System Tournament <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: XL</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Klasher, I want to enter a Swiss System tournament so that I am paired with opponents of similar skill throughout the competition.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Round 1 random pairing
Given a Swiss tournament has started
When Round 1 pairings are generated
Then all participants shall be randomly paired

Scenario: Subsequent round pairing by score
Given Round 1 of a Swiss tournament has completed
When Round 2 pairings are generated
Then winners shall be paired against other winners and losers against other losers
And the system shall avoid rematches where possible

Scenario: Tournament completion
Given all predetermined rounds have been completed (e.g. 5 rounds for 32 players)
When the final round concludes
Then the system shall display final standings ranked by score</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F32, F33</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Gaming Doc</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F60 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F60 — Single Elimination Tournament <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: L</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Klasher, I want to enter a Single Elimination tournament so that a champion is determined efficiently.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Elimination on loss
Given a Single Elimination tournament is in progress
When a Klasher loses a match
Then they shall be immediately eliminated from the tournament
And shall no longer be eligible for further competitive matches in that tournament

Scenario: Bracket progression
Given a match in the elimination bracket has concluded
When the result is confirmed
Then the winner shall advance to the next round bracket position automatically
And the bracket display shall update to reflect the new state

Scenario: Champion determined
Given the final match of the tournament has been completed
When the result is confirmed
Then the last remaining undefeated Klasher shall be declared the tournament champion</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F32, F33</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Gaming Doc</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F61 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F61 — Double Elimination Tournament (Phase 2 — Deferred) <span class="badge badge-wont-have">WON'T HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: XL</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Klasher, I want to enter a Double Elimination tournament so that I have a second chance after my first loss.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Deferred to Phase 2 — not in scope for current development.</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F60</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Gaming Doc</p>

                <p><strong>Phase 2 Note:</strong> Explicitly deferred to Phase 2. A losers bracket must run in parallel with the winners bracket. This significantly increases system complexity.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F62 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F62 — Free-For-All Klash Format <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: XL</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Klasher, I want to enter a Free-For-All klash so that I can compete against all participants simultaneously with no teams.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: FFA game in progress
Given a Free-For-All klash has started
When the game is running
Then every participant shall compete against every other participant with no team structure
And a maximum of 3 Nudge Plays shall be available per participant (see F57)

Scenario: FFA winner determined
Given the FFA timer has expired
When the system calculates the result
Then the participant with the highest score (most wins or eliminations — TBD) shall be declared the winner</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F32, F33, F57</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Gaming Doc</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-3"><strong>Epic 4 Summary:</strong> 5 user stories • 2 Must Have, 2 Should Have, 1 Won't Have (Phase 2) • Builds structured tournament formats beyond one-on-one klashes</p>
        <hr class="mt-4 mb-4">

        <!-- Epic 5: User Profile & Social Feed -->
        <h4 id="epic-5-stories" class="mt-4">Epic 5: User Profile & Social Feed</h4>
        <p class="text-muted">User profiles, stats display, follow/unfollow, personalised news feed, and quick-access UI elements.</p>

        <!-- F17 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F17 — User Profile Page with Stats and Customisation <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: L</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a user, I want a profile page displaying my Klasher name, profile picture, background image, and stats so that other users can identify and learn about me.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Profile page loads with all fields
Given a user navigates to a public profile
When the profile page loads
Then the system shall display: Klasher name, profile picture, background image, total klashes, wins, losses, draws, follower count, and following count

Scenario: User customises their profile picture
Given a logged-in user is on their own profile
When they upload a new profile picture
Then the system shall update the displayed profile picture immediately</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F01</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F18 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F18 — Follow/Unfollow System <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a user, I want to follow other Klashers so that I can stay connected with users I find interesting.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: User follows another Klasher
Given a user is viewing a public profile
When they tap the Follow button
Then the system shall add that Klasher to their following list
And the followed Klasher's follower count shall increment by 1 in real time

Scenario: User unfollows a Klasher
Given a user is viewing a profile they currently follow
When they tap the Unfollow button
Then the Klasher shall be removed from their following list
And the follower count shall decrement by 1 in real time</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F01</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F19 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F19 — Personalised News Feed <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: L</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a user, I want a news feed on my profile so that I can discover upcoming klashes, top Klashers, new music, and KO organised events.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: News feed loads with all sections
Given a user is on their profile page
When the feed section loads
Then the system shall display dynamically updated sections including: new music suggestions, upcoming klashes, top Klashers, top 40 independent chart, and KO-organised klashes

Scenario: Feed updates in real time
Given a new event (e.g. a klash going live) occurs
When the event is published
Then the relevant feed section shall update without requiring a full page refresh</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F17, F18</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F20 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F20 — Klash Box Quick Access <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a user, I want a Klash Box visible in the corner of my profile page so that I can quickly access klashing from anywhere on my profile.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Klash Box is persistently visible
Given a user is on their profile page
When they scroll or navigate within the profile
Then the Klash Box shall remain persistently displayed in the bottom-left corner of the screen at all times

Scenario: Klash Box opens klash flow
Given a user taps the Klash Box
When the tap is registered
Then the system shall open the klash initiation flow (genre and duration selection)</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F17</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-3"><strong>Epic 5 Summary:</strong> 4 user stories • 2 Must Have, 2 Should Have • Builds user identity, social connections, and content discovery</p>
        <hr class="mt-4 mb-4">

        <!-- Epic 6: Messaging -->
        <h4 id="epic-6-stories" class="mt-4">Epic 6: Messaging</h4>
        <p class="text-muted">Real-time instant messaging with delivery and read receipts for user-to-user communication.</p>

        <!-- F21 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F21 — Real-Time Instant Messaging <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: L</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a user, I want to send and receive instant messages with other users so that I can communicate in real time.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Message delivered in real time
Given two users are both online
When User A sends a message to User B
Then the message shall appear in User B's message thread in real time without a page refresh
And a delivery receipt shall be shown to User A

Scenario: Read receipt displayed
Given User B has opened and read a message from User A
When User B reads the message
Then a read receipt shall be displayed to User A

Scenario: Message history persisted
Given a user navigates away from a message thread and returns
When they reopen the thread
Then the full message history shall be displayed</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F01</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-3"><strong>Epic 6 Summary:</strong> 1 user story • Must Have • Enables direct user-to-user communication</p>
        <hr class="mt-4 mb-4">

        <!-- Epic 7: Playlist Management -->
        <h4 id="epic-7-stories" class="mt-4">Epic 7: Playlist Management</h4>
        <p class="text-muted">Playlist creation, track management, klash playlist preparation, and playlist sharing.</p>

        <!-- F22 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F22 — Create and Manage Playlists <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a user, I want to create playlists from songs in my library so that I can organise my music by mood or preference.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: User creates a new playlist
Given a logged-in user is in their library
When they create a new playlist and give it a name
Then the system shall create the playlist and display it in their playlist list

Scenario: User adds a track to a playlist
Given a playlist exists
When the user adds a track
Then the track shall appear in the playlist and be reorderable
And the user shall be able to remove tracks from the playlist

Scenario: Playlist name required
Given a user attempts to create a playlist without a name
When they submit the creation form
Then the system shall reject the creation and display a name-required error</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F05, F06</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F23 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F23 — Klash Playlist Preparation <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a user, I want to prepare a dedicated klash playlist so that I have my chosen tracks ready before a klash begins.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Klash playlist created and selected at setup
Given a user has created a playlist designated as a klash playlist
When they enter the klash song selection screen
Then the klash playlist shall be available as a selectable source
And tracks shall play in order or shuffle (user preference TBD with Lincoln)

Scenario: Klash playlist distinct from standard playlist
Given a user is creating a playlist
When they designate it as a klash playlist
Then the system shall distinguish it from standard playlists in the UI</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F22</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F24 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F24 — Share Playlists with Other Users <span class="badge badge-could-have">COULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a user, I want to share my playlists with other users so that I can show them my favourite music.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: User shares a playlist publicly
Given a user has a playlist they want to share
When they toggle the playlist to Public
Then the playlist shall appear on their public profile and be visible to other users

Scenario: Another user saves a shared playlist
Given a user is viewing a shared playlist on another Klasher's profile
When they tap Save Playlist
Then a copy of that playlist shall be added to their own library</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F22, F17</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-3"><strong>Epic 7 Summary:</strong> 3 user stories • 2 Must Have, 1 Could Have • Enables music organisation and sharing</p>
        <hr class="mt-4 mb-4">

        <!-- Epic 8: Klash Coin & Wallet -->
        <h4 id="epic-8-stories" class="mt-4">Epic 8: Klash Coin & Wallet</h4>
        <p class="text-muted">The platform economy: wallet management, coin purchases, gifting, earning, spending, and cash-out functionality.</p>

        <!-- F25 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F25 — Klash Coin Balance Display <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a user, I want a Klash Coin balance displayed on my profile so that I can see how many coins I have at any time.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Coin balance displayed
Given a logged-in user views their profile
When the profile loads
Then the current Klash Coin balance shall be prominently displayed
And the balance shall reflect the most recent completed transaction

Scenario: Balance updates after transaction
Given a user has just completed a coin transaction (purchase, gift, spend)
When the transaction is confirmed
Then the displayed balance shall update immediately without requiring a page refresh</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F17</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F26 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F26 — Earn Coins on Win (Threshold-Based) <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: L</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Klasher, I want to earn Klash Coins through klashing once I reach 1,000 followers and 1,000 wins so that sustained achievement is rewarded.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Eligible Klasher earns coins after a win
Given a Klasher has at least 1,000 followers and 1,000 wins
When they win a klash
Then the system shall credit their Klash Coin wallet with the defined coin reward

Scenario: Progress shown to ineligible Klasher
Given a Klasher has fewer than 1,000 followers or 1,000 wins
When they view the coin eligibility section of their profile
Then the system shall display their current progress toward both thresholds</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F14, F18, F25</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F27 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F27 — Independent Klasher Unrestricted Transactions <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As an Independent Klasher, I want to send and receive Klash Coins immediately upon account creation so that I can transact without restrictions.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Independent Klasher transacts without threshold
Given a user with the Independent Klasher tier is logged in
When they attempt to send or receive Klash Coins
Then the system shall permit the transaction without checking follower or win thresholds</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F04, F25</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F28 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F28 — Gift Klash Coins to Other Users <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a user, I want to gift Klash Coins to other users so that I can reward or support Klashers I enjoy.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Successful coin gift
Given a user has a sufficient Klash Coin balance
When they initiate a gift to another user, specify the recipient and amount, and confirm
Then the sender's balance shall decrease by the gifted amount immediately
And the recipient's balance shall increase by the gifted amount immediately
And both parties shall receive a transaction notification

Scenario: Insufficient balance
Given a user attempts to gift more coins than their current balance
When they confirm the gift
Then the system shall reject the transaction and display an insufficient funds message</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F25</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F29 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F29 — Super Klasher Host Revenue Share <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: L</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Super Klasher, I want to automatically receive a percentage of revenue from every klash I organise so that my hosting efforts are compensated.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Host fee credited after klash completion
Given a Super Klasher has organised a klash with a joining fee
When the klash concludes and results are confirmed
Then the system shall calculate the Super Klasher's host percentage of the total pot
And credit that amount to their Klash Coin wallet automatically
And generate a transaction record showing the calculation

Scenario: Remaining pot distributed to winners
Given the host fee has been deducted
When the distribution is processed
Then the remaining pot shall be distributed to 1st, 2nd, and 3rd place klashers according to the defined split</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F04, F13, F25</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> BRD</p>

                <div class="alert alert-warning">
                    <strong>⚠️ Open Item Q14:</strong> Host fee percentage and winner distribution split to be confirmed with Lincoln.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F46 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F46 — Self-Custody Klash Coin Wallet <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: L</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a user, I want a self-custody Klash Coin wallet within my account so that I can manage all my digital assets on the platform.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Wallet accessible from account
Given a logged-in user navigates to their wallet
When the wallet screen loads
Then the system shall display: current coin balance, full transaction history (chronological), and available actions (purchase, cash out, gift)

Scenario: Wallet is unique per user
Given two different users are logged in
When either user views their wallet
Then they shall only see their own balance and transaction history</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F01</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Wallet & Coin Doc</p>

                <p><strong>Regulatory Note:</strong> See Domain Requirement D02 for the regulatory implications of this feature.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F47 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F47 — Purchase Klash Coins via Card <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: L</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a user, I want to purchase Klash Coins using a credit or debit card so that I can credit my wallet and participate in paid features.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Successful coin purchase
Given a user is on the coin purchase screen
When they select an amount, enter valid card details, and confirm
Then the system shall process the payment via the payment processor
And credit the purchased coins to the user's wallet immediately upon payment confirmation
And display a purchase confirmation

Scenario: Failed payment
Given a user attempts to purchase coins with invalid or declined card details
When the payment processor returns a failure
Then the system shall display an appropriate error message
And no coins shall be credited to the wallet

Scenario: Card data handling
Given a user is entering card details
When they submit payment information
Then card details shall be handled entirely by the regulated payment processor
And shall never be stored on KO's own servers</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F46</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Wallet & Coin Doc</p>

                <p><strong>Regulatory Note:</strong> See Domain Requirements D02 and D03 for regulatory and app store policy constraints.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F48 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F48 — Automatic Wallet Debit for In-App Transactions <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a user, I want my Klash Coin wallet to automatically debit when I make an in-app transaction so that payments are seamless and require no manual steps.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Automatic debit on in-app transaction
Given a user activates a paid feature (Go Live, Nudge, music purchase)
When the activation is confirmed
Then the system shall debit the exact cost from the user's wallet automatically
And display the updated balance immediately
And create a transaction record

Scenario: Insufficient balance blocks transaction
Given a user attempts to activate a paid feature
When their wallet balance is insufficient to cover the cost
Then the system shall block the activation and prompt the user to purchase more coins</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F46</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Wallet & Coin Doc</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F49 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F49 — Context-Based Coin Gifting (In-Klash, Profile, Music) <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a user, I want to gift Klash Coins to another user during a klash, while listening to music, or when liking a profile so that I can reward klashers I enjoy in the moment.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: In-klash coin gifting
Given a klash is in progress and a user (Klasher or spectator) has sufficient coins
When they initiate a gift to a participant
Then the gift flow shall prompt for amount confirmation
And on confirmation shall debit the sender and credit the recipient immediately
And both parties shall receive a notification

Scenario: Gifting from profile/music context
Given a user is viewing a Klasher's profile or listening to music
When they tap the gift icon and confirm an amount
Then the same debit/credit flow shall execute as above</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F46, F28</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Wallet & Coin Doc</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F50 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F50 — Purchase Tracks via Klash Coin Wallet <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: L</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a user, I want to purchase music I discover within KO using my Klash Coin wallet so that I can buy tracks without leaving the app.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: User purchases a track
Given a user is listening to a track in the KO library
When they tap the purchase button and confirm
Then the system shall debit the track cost from their wallet
And credit the equivalent amount to the artist's wallet
And add the purchased track automatically to the user's preferred playlist
And display a purchase confirmation

Scenario: Purchase button absent on non-purchasable track
Given a track has not been made available for purchase by its owner
When a user views that track
Then no purchase button shall be displayed</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F46, F22</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Wallet & Coin Doc</p>

                <p><strong>Technical Note:</strong> Track pricing mechanism and how artists set prices to be confirmed with Lincoln.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F51 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F51 — Cash Out Klash Coins to Bank Account <span class="badge badge-must-have">MUST HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: XL</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a user, I want to cash out my Klash Coin earnings into my local currency so that I can access real money from my in-app activity.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Successful cash out
Given a user has a Klash Coin balance above the minimum cash-out threshold (TBD)
When they initiate a cash out, specify the amount, and confirm their bank details
Then the system shall debit the specified coins from their wallet
And initiate a transfer of the equivalent fiat amount to their nominated bank account
And display a confirmation with an estimated transfer time

Scenario: Cash out below minimum threshold
Given a user attempts to cash out an amount below the minimum threshold
When they submit the request
Then the system shall reject it and display the minimum cash-out requirement

Scenario: Identity verification required
Given a user is cashing out above the KYC threshold (amount TBD per AML requirements)
When they initiate the cash out
Then the system shall require identity verification before processing the transfer</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F46</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Wallet & Coin Doc</p>

                <p><strong>Regulatory Note:</strong> See Domain Requirement D02 — cash out may require FCA authorisation. Minimum threshold, processing time, and KYC threshold to be confirmed with Lincoln's legal advisors.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F52 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F52 — Super Klasher Pot Management & Distribution <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: XL</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Super Klasher, I want participant joining fees to be pooled and distributed to winners and the host automatically so that the staking economy works fairly.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Joining fee collected from each participant
Given a Super Klasher has set a joining fee and a participant joins
When the participant confirms entry
Then the joining fee shall be debited from the participant's wallet immediately
And deposited into the klash's pot fund (escrow)

Scenario: Pot distributed on klash completion
Given the klash has concluded and results are confirmed
When the distribution is processed
Then the Super Klasher's host percentage shall be credited to their wallet first
And the remaining pot shall be distributed to 1st, 2nd, and 3rd place finishers according to the defined split
And all distributions shall be credited immediately with individual transaction records

Scenario: Klash cancelled before completion
Given a Super Klasher klash is cancelled before completion
When the cancellation is confirmed
Then all joining fees shall be refunded to participants' wallets in full</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F46, F13, F29</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Wallet & Coin Doc</p>

                <p><strong>Technical Note:</strong> Distribution percentages to be confirmed with Lincoln.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-3"><strong>Epic 8 Summary:</strong> 12 user stories • 6 Must Have, 5 Should Have, 1 Could Have • Builds the complete platform economy from wallet creation through purchase, gifting, earning, spending, and cash-out</p>
        <hr class="mt-4 mb-4">

        <!-- Epic 9: Go Live -->
        <h4 id="epic-9-stories" class="mt-4">Epic 9: Go Live</h4>
        <p class="text-muted">Live video and audio streaming during klashes and standalone showcase performances.</p>

        <!-- F53 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F53 — Go Live Activation During Klash <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: L</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Klasher, I want to activate Go Live during a klash so that my opponent and spectators can see and hear me reacting in real time.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Go Live activated mid-klash
Given a klash has been in progress for more than 10 seconds
And the klash has more than 10 seconds remaining
And the user has sufficient Klash Coins
When the user taps the Go Live button
Then the system shall debit the Go Live cost from their wallet automatically
And begin streaming the user's camera and audio to the opponent and all spectators immediately

Scenario: Go Live blocked in first 10 seconds
Given a klash has been in progress for fewer than 10 seconds
When the user attempts to activate Go Live
Then the system shall prevent activation and display a message indicating the timing restriction

Scenario: Go Live blocked in last 10 seconds
Given a klash has fewer than 10 seconds remaining
When the user attempts to activate Go Live
Then the system shall prevent activation and display a message indicating the timing restriction

Scenario: Insufficient balance
Given a user attempts to activate Go Live
When their wallet balance is insufficient
Then the system shall block activation and prompt a coin purchase</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F46, F48</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Wallet & Coin Doc</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F54 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F54 — Pre-Klash Go Live Purchase <span class="badge badge-could-have">COULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Klasher, I want to purchase Go Live before a klash begins so that I have it ready to activate when needed.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Pre-klash Go Live purchase
Given a user is on their profile or the pre-klash screen
When they purchase Go Live
Then the coin transaction shall be processed immediately
And a Go Live credit shall be stored against their account for use in the next klash
And the Go Live button shall be shown as available when the klash begins</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F46, F53</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Wallet & Coin Doc</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F55 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F55 — Go Live Showcase for Independent Klashers <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: XL</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As an Independent Klasher, I want to activate Go Live Showcase to perform live to an audience so that I can grow my visibility and earn coins.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Go Live Showcase purchased and activated
Given an Independent Klasher has purchased a Go Live Showcase session
When they activate it via the Go Live Showcase button
Then the system shall begin streaming their live performance to the KO audience
And the performance shall be listed as a live event in the Forums and news feed

Scenario: Audience can view and gift coins during Showcase
Given a Go Live Showcase is in progress
When audience members view the performance
Then they shall be able to gift Klash Coins to the performing artist in real time

Scenario: Go Live Showcase purchase required before activation
Given an Independent Klasher has not purchased a Showcase session
When they attempt to activate Go Live Showcase
Then the system shall prompt them to purchase before proceeding</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F46, F07, F54</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Wallet & Coin Doc</p>

                <div class="alert alert-warning">
                    <strong>⚠️ Open Item Q12:</strong> Audience monetisation mechanism, showcase duration limits, and discovery/listing behaviour to be confirmed with Lincoln.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-3"><strong>Epic 9 Summary:</strong> 3 user stories • 2 Should Have, 1 Could Have • Enables live video streaming during competition and showcase performances</p>
        <hr class="mt-4 mb-4">

        <!-- Epic 10: Nudge Play -->
        <h4 id="epic-10-stories" class="mt-4">Epic 10: Nudge Play</h4>
        <p class="text-muted">Tactical disruption mechanic available for purchase during klashes with specific timing constraints.</p>

        <!-- F56 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F56 — Nudge Play Tactical Disruption (60/90 Sec Klashes) <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: L</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Klasher in a 60 or 90 second klash, I want to use a Nudge Play to disrupt my opponent so that I gain a tactical advantage.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Nudge activated within valid window
Given a 60 or 90 second klash is in progress
And more than 10 seconds have elapsed
And more than 10 seconds remain
And the user has sufficient coins
When the user activates Nudge Play
Then the system shall debit the Nudge cost from their wallet
And execute the Nudge mechanic against the opponent (mechanic TBD with Lincoln)

Scenario: Nudge blocked outside valid window
Given a klash has fewer than 10 seconds remaining or fewer than 10 seconds have elapsed
When a user attempts to activate Nudge
Then the system shall prevent activation and display the timing restriction message

Scenario: Nudge unavailable in 30-second klash
Given a 30-second klash is in progress
When a user views the Nudge button
Then the Nudge button shall be disabled or hidden
And a tooltip shall explain it is unavailable for this duration</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F46, F48, F31</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Wallet & Coin Doc</p>

                <div class="alert alert-warning">
                    <strong>⚠️ Open Item Q1:</strong> The exact mechanic and effect of Nudge Play is the most critical undefined item in this document — must be confirmed with Lincoln before this feature can be designed.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F57 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F57 — Nudge Play in Free-For-All (3-Use Cap) <span class="badge badge-could-have">COULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: L</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a Klasher in a Free-For-All klash, I want to use up to 3 Nudge Plays during the game so that I have multiple tactical disruption opportunities.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: FFA Nudge within 3-use cap
Given a Free-For-All klash is in progress
When a user activates Nudge
Then the system shall decrement their available nudge count from the 3-use maximum
And execute the Nudge mechanic

Scenario: FFA Nudge cap reached
Given a user has used all 3 available Nudge Plays in an FFA klash
When they attempt to activate Nudge again
Then the system shall prevent further activation and display a "Nudge limit reached" message</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F56, F62</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Gaming Doc</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-3"><strong>Epic 10 Summary:</strong> 2 user stories • 1 Should Have, 1 Could Have • Adds tactical gameplay mechanic for disruption during competition</p>
        <hr class="mt-4 mb-4">

        <!-- Epic 11: Forums & Discovery -->
        <h4 id="epic-11-stories" class="mt-4">Epic 11: Forums & Discovery</h4>
        <p class="text-muted">Discovery and browsing of live and archived klashes with filtering and state management.</p>

        <!-- F63 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F63 — Join Random Klash from Forums <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a user, I want to join a random klash from the Forums so that I can discover new competitions without searching.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Random klash joined
Given a user is in the Forums
When they tap "Join Random Klash"
Then the system shall select an available live klash and place the user into it as a participant or spectator
And display the klash details (genre, duration, participants) before confirming entry</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F01, F32</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Gaming Doc</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F64 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F64 — Browse Live Klashes in Forums <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: L</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a user, I want to browse all live klashes in the Forums so that I can find and join or spectate active competitions.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Live klash list displayed
Given a user navigates to the Forums
When the page loads
Then the system shall display all currently live klashes
And each listing shall show: genre, duration format, participant names, and current status
And all displayed klashes shall have a time remaining within the 24-hour window</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F01</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Gaming Doc</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F65 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F65 — Filter Klashes by Genre in Forums <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a user, I want to browse klashes by genre in the Forums so that I can find competitions in music styles I prefer.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Genre filter applied
Given a user is in the Forums
When they select a genre filter (e.g. Hip-Hop)
Then the system shall display only live klashes within that klash space
And the listing shall update without a full page reload</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F30, F64</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Gaming Doc</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F66 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F66 — Place Klash on Hold (State Serialisation) <span class="badge badge-could-have">COULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: XL</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a user, I want to put a klash on hold and return to it later so that I can pause participation without losing my place.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Klash placed on hold
Given a klash is in progress and both participants agree to pause
When a hold is requested and confirmed by both parties
Then the system shall preserve the complete klash state
And the klash shall remain listed in the Forums as "On Hold"

Scenario: Klash resumed
Given a klash is on hold
When both participants return and confirm resumption
Then the system shall restore the klash state and resume from the paused point

Scenario: Hold expires
Given a klash has been on hold for longer than the maximum hold duration (TBD with Lincoln)
When the hold duration expires
Then the system shall cancel the klash and notify both participants</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F64</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Gaming Doc</p>

                <div class="alert alert-warning">
                    <strong>⚠️ Open Item Q6:</strong> Maximum hold duration and whether hold requires mutual consent from both participants to be confirmed with Lincoln.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F67 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F67 — Browse 24-Hour Klash Archive <span class="badge badge-could-have">COULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: L</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a user, I want to review klashes from the last 24 hours in the Forums so that I can catch up on competitions I missed.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: 24-hour archive browsed
Given a user navigates to the archive section of the Forums
When they browse completed klashes
Then the system shall display all klashes completed within the last 24 hours
And each entry shall be filterable by: genre, Super Klasher, KO organised, Klasher, Independent Klasher
And entries shall show: result, participants, tracks used

Scenario: Archive entries expire
Given a klash was completed more than 24 hours ago
When the expiry process runs
Then that klash shall no longer appear in the archive listing</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F64</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Gaming Doc</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-3"><strong>Epic 11 Summary:</strong> 5 user stories • 3 Should Have, 2 Could Have • Enables discovery, browsing, and archiving of klash content</p>
        <hr class="mt-4 mb-4">

        <!-- Epic 12: Music Social -->
        <h4 id="epic-12-stories" class="mt-4">Epic 12: Music Social</h4>
        <p class="text-muted">Music-based social features including snippet messages, emotion-based suggestions, recommendations, and independent artist discovery.</p>

        <!-- F68 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F68 — Send Song Snippet as Emotion Message <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: L</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a user, I want to send a song snippet to another user as a message so that I can express a feeling or emotion through music.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: User sends a music message
Given a user is in a message thread with another user
When they select a track, choose a snippet, optionally tag an emotion (e.g. Happy, Angry, In Love, Sorrow, Thanks, Birthday), and send
Then the snippet message shall appear in the thread as a playable audio snippet — not the full track
And the recipient shall be able to play the snippet directly within the message thread

Scenario: Full track not sent
Given a user is composing a music message
When they select a track
Then the system shall only allow a snippet (not the full track) to be sent
And the snippet duration limits shall match platform-defined snippet lengths</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F21, F05</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Gaming Doc</p>

                <p><strong>Technical Note:</strong> Exact snippet duration for music messages and the definitive list of emotion tags to be confirmed with Lincoln.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F69 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F69 — Emotion-Based Music Suggestions <span class="badge badge-could-have">COULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: L</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a user, I want my playlist to suggest songs relevant to my current emotion so that I can quickly find music that fits how I feel.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Emotion-based suggestion returned
Given a user selects an emotion or moment type from the suggestion prompt (e.g. Happy)
When the system processes the selection
Then the system shall return a list of tracks relevant to that emotion
And suggestions shall draw from both the KO library and the user's own library</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F22, F68</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Gaming Doc</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F70 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F70 — Music Recommendations (Up to 100 Tracks) <span class="badge badge-could-have">COULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: L</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a user, I want to receive up to 100 music recommendations outside my existing playlist so that I can discover new music.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Recommendations displayed in feed
Given a user is on their social or discovery feed
When the recommendations section loads
Then the system shall display up to 100 track recommendations not already in the user's library
And recommendations shall be based on listening history, klash history, or genre preferences</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F22, F19</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Gaming Doc</p>

                <p><strong>Technical Note:</strong> Recommendation algorithm to be confirmed with Lincoln. The 100 recommendation limit is subject to change. A rule-based approach is recommended for Phase 2 launch, with ML-based recommendations as a future iteration.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- F71 -->
        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
                <h5 class="mb-0">F71 — Independent Artist Music Discovery & Support <span class="badge badge-should-have">SHOULD HAVE</span> <span class="badge" style="background-color: #6c757d; color: white;">Weight: M</span></h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p><strong>User Story:</strong><br>
                As a user, I want to interact with Independent music content in the social feed so that I can discover and support independent artists.</p>

                <p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>
                <pre><code class="language-gherkin">Scenario: Independent music visible in social feed
Given a user is browsing the social feed
When independent artist content is surfaced
Then the user shall be able to like, share, and purchase independent tracks directly from the feed

Scenario: Independent artist visible in charts
Given an Independent Klasher has uploaded and distributed tracks
When the charts are calculated
Then eligible tracks shall appear in the independent charts section</code></pre>

                <p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> F07, F19, F50</p>
                <p><strong>Source:</strong> Gaming Doc</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-3"><strong>Epic 12 Summary:</strong> 4 user stories • 2 Should Have, 2 Could Have • Adds music-centric social interaction and discovery features</p>
        <hr class="mt-4 mb-4">

